1
00:02:09,185 --> 00:02:11,245
Episode 95

2
00:02:11,825 --> 00:02:15,365
2 months after
the Conquest of İnegöl

3
00:02:16,505 --> 00:02:19,005
Just like the old days, my love.

4
00:02:19,705 --> 00:02:22,285
The one who loves the most,
runs the fastest.

5
00:02:23,125 --> 00:02:24,845
Karayel!

6
00:02:25,665 --> 00:02:31,885
Do you hear it? Huh?
What do they say to us?

7
00:02:33,425 --> 00:02:37,605
But they don't know that...

8
00:02:37,885 --> 00:02:40,685
we become the wind and howl
everywhere for love!

9
00:02:42,205 --> 00:02:44,525
Show it then, Osman Bey.

10
00:02:44,945 --> 00:02:47,265
Alaca is still strong.

11
00:02:49,725 --> 00:02:51,765
She can go through the wind.

12
00:02:52,565 --> 00:02:54,065
Keep that in mind.

13
00:02:57,205 --> 00:02:59,325
Karayel suffered a lot for us.

14
00:02:59,965 --> 00:03:04,325
But now we have İltutan.

15
00:03:04,925 --> 00:03:07,325
İltutan is fast too.

16
00:03:09,025 --> 00:03:14,345
His renown makes a home out
of the lands he runs through.

17
00:03:17,145 --> 00:03:19,145
Once he eats Alaca's dusts...

18
00:03:20,045 --> 00:03:22,605
I hope it won't lose his speed.

19
00:03:23,445 --> 00:03:24,965
That's what you say?

20
00:03:26,685 --> 00:03:30,345
Then, Cerkutay!

21
00:03:35,845 --> 00:03:37,925
Oh, Cerkutay.

22
00:03:42,845 --> 00:03:44,805
I should give these weapons
to you.

23
00:03:44,845 --> 00:03:47,345
You know, they'll make
me heavier.

24
00:03:47,805 --> 00:03:49,525
I need to be faster.

25
00:03:52,645 --> 00:03:56,425
For speed, you give up on your
weapons, Osman.

26
00:03:56,825 --> 00:03:58,925
It's that important, huh?

27
00:03:59,305 --> 00:04:02,445
It's important.

28
00:04:05,185 --> 00:04:08,525
Then, we should let
our horses speak.

29
00:04:09,525 --> 00:04:13,185
We won't stop until that greens.

30
00:04:16,885 --> 00:04:20,765
Alaca, don't let me down.

31
00:04:23,245 --> 00:04:24,665
İltutan.

32
00:04:25,085 --> 00:04:26,705
Come on, son.

33
00:04:27,445 --> 00:04:28,925
Come on, then!

34
00:04:29,805 --> 00:04:31,965
Let's become wind for love!

35
00:04:32,445 --> 00:04:33,905
Come on!

36
00:05:14,705 --> 00:05:16,245
İltutan!

37
00:05:16,265 --> 00:05:18,765
No one knows the mind of your
owner better than you!

38
00:05:18,805 --> 00:05:20,525
Come on, don't disappoint me.

39
00:05:27,145 --> 00:05:30,245
Alaca! If you get behind,
your white hair will get dust!

40
00:05:30,265 --> 00:05:31,265
Speed up!

41
00:05:31,265 --> 00:05:33,365
Let's not pollute our love.

42
00:06:10,745 --> 00:06:11,925
Bala.

43
00:06:12,695 --> 00:06:14,565
You are a good rider.

44
00:06:14,665 --> 00:06:16,145
Thank you, my bey.

45
00:06:21,265 --> 00:06:22,785
Come on.

46
00:06:55,885 --> 00:06:58,065
So, we are even again, Osman?

47
00:06:59,405 --> 00:07:02,425
Just like our love, Bala.

48
00:07:04,625 --> 00:07:06,725
Mashallah to İltutan.

49
00:07:07,565 --> 00:07:10,725
He's been carrying you
for a time now.

50
00:07:11,745 --> 00:07:14,125
Let's sit here.

51
00:07:24,045 --> 00:07:26,225
We have many supporters.

52
00:07:26,805 --> 00:07:31,525
Our brothers, alps, horses.
But...

53
00:07:33,565 --> 00:07:35,745
there is none like the strength of
the house.

54
00:07:36,865 --> 00:07:42,265
My heart is filled with the love
of my children and jihad.

55
00:07:44,065 --> 00:07:46,345
But you are always behind me.

56
00:07:46,665 --> 00:07:48,745
May Allah protect you.

57
00:07:49,015 --> 00:07:52,845
I face all these hardships because
of your love.

58
00:07:53,665 --> 00:07:55,705
I get my strength from you.

59
00:07:56,005 --> 00:07:59,505
May Allah protect you
and our children.

60
00:07:59,585 --> 00:08:01,145
Amin.

61
00:08:01,325 --> 00:08:02,885
Amin.

62
00:08:03,045 --> 00:08:06,445
May Allah keep us together.

63
00:08:07,665 --> 00:08:09,245
Amin.

64
00:08:09,945 --> 00:08:11,465
Amin.

65
00:08:22,350 --> 00:08:23,860
Take off your hand!

66
00:08:23,940 --> 00:08:25,760
We need horses!

67
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:27,700
And some gold!

68
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:30,500
It appears that you have both.

69
00:08:38,400 --> 00:08:40,120
Is that so?

70
00:08:45,220 --> 00:08:47,440
Come, then.

71
00:08:54,060 --> 00:08:55,620
Come.

72
00:08:56,760 --> 00:08:59,020
Come and get beaten.

73
00:08:59,040 --> 00:09:00,560
You are brave.

74
00:09:00,700 --> 00:09:02,700
Brave people don't live long.

75
00:09:03,660 --> 00:09:05,360
Do as we say...

76
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:08,300
and we might spare your life.

77
00:09:08,420 --> 00:09:12,080
It's been a while since we mounted
to face the winds, my bey.

78
00:09:13,280 --> 00:09:17,560
And it's been a while since we've
beaten their kind.

79
00:09:18,060 --> 00:09:20,060
Don't hold me back.

80
00:09:22,620 --> 00:09:24,360
As you wish.

81
00:09:25,380 --> 00:09:26,960
Come on, then!

82
00:09:30,300 --> 00:09:31,880
Bala!

83
00:09:56,580 --> 00:09:57,860
Are you alright?

84
00:09:58,640 --> 00:10:00,080
I am, Osman.

85
00:10:00,460 --> 00:10:02,580
Come on! Come on!

86
00:10:03,760 --> 00:10:05,300
My bey!

87
00:10:19,080 --> 00:10:20,660
My bey.

88
00:10:20,940 --> 00:10:22,660
Are you alright?

89
00:10:24,520 --> 00:10:27,580
My bey, your horses don't run.
They fly!

90
00:10:27,900 --> 00:10:29,640
We couldn't come in time!

91
00:10:33,130 --> 00:10:34,650
Dogs!

92
00:10:34,860 --> 00:10:36,670
They made a mistake.

93
00:10:37,360 --> 00:10:39,400
They didn't know who you are.

94
00:10:39,580 --> 00:10:41,340
Don't worry.

95
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:44,020
They can't bite us.

96
00:10:45,980 --> 00:10:47,820
Return to the tribe.

97
00:10:48,460 --> 00:10:52,240
Then, you'll find out where
did they come from.

98
00:10:52,240 --> 00:10:53,300
Yes, my bey.

99
00:10:53,300 --> 00:10:54,780
Stay safe, my bey.

100
00:10:54,980 --> 00:10:56,220
You too.

101
00:10:57,140 --> 00:10:58,300
Thank you.

102
00:10:58,380 --> 00:10:59,880
-My bey.
-Come on.

103
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:01,540
Come on.

104
00:11:23,340 --> 00:11:25,860
Caravansarai on the road

105
00:12:01,785 --> 00:12:03,125
Sit.

106
00:12:03,385 --> 00:12:05,085
Don't stand.

107
00:12:05,905 --> 00:12:09,285
Our table is always open to guests.

108
00:12:09,285 --> 00:12:12,285
The only thing I want to
see on your table...

109
00:12:15,245 --> 00:12:17,265
is Osman's head.

110
00:12:23,005 --> 00:12:24,725
Don't hurry.

111
00:12:27,825 --> 00:12:29,525
Everything has a time.

112
00:12:30,905 --> 00:12:33,045
Can someone reach victory
without patience?

113
00:12:33,585 --> 00:12:36,405
Don't speak like your idiot master
Darius!

114
00:12:37,425 --> 00:12:39,505
He loved waiting.

115
00:12:41,125 --> 00:12:42,345
Nikola too.

116
00:12:43,885 --> 00:12:46,425
They are all in their graves now.

117
00:12:57,705 --> 00:13:01,425
I waited but did not face
the enemy...

118
00:13:02,545 --> 00:13:04,445
but I stood beside him.

119
00:13:05,885 --> 00:13:07,725
I stood behind him.

120
00:13:08,985 --> 00:13:11,105
I gained his trust.

121
00:13:33,045 --> 00:13:38,205
Why is Kayı's banner bigger
than the others?

122
00:13:39,345 --> 00:13:41,345
It wasn't like this before.

123
00:13:42,445 --> 00:13:46,325
The answer to the question is
in the question, my bey.

124
00:13:47,105 --> 00:13:48,965
It wasn't like this.

125
00:13:49,605 --> 00:13:52,545
As Kayı grows,
so does its banner.

126
00:13:52,605 --> 00:13:55,605
Until it expands to the
whole world.

127
00:13:56,825 --> 00:13:59,385
But don't forget...

128
00:14:00,575 --> 00:14:03,625
with its might,
so grows its problems.

129
00:14:04,905 --> 00:14:06,285
Thank you.

130
00:14:06,765 --> 00:14:08,145
Come.

131
00:14:14,225 --> 00:14:15,565
Salam Alaikum.

132
00:14:15,565 --> 00:14:17,445
Alaikum Salam.

133
00:14:22,285 --> 00:14:24,125
Come, Osman Bey.

134
00:14:34,625 --> 00:14:35,705
Thank you.

135
00:14:45,805 --> 00:14:52,445
We heard that Turkmens are flowing to
the West after the conquest.

136
00:14:53,125 --> 00:14:58,385
Because they see İnegöl and Bilecik
as home.

137
00:14:58,565 --> 00:15:00,385
They love you.

138
00:15:00,385 --> 00:15:02,145
Thank you.
Thank you.

139
00:15:03,465 --> 00:15:06,565
That's we do conquest.

140
00:15:07,565 --> 00:15:12,685
There won't be a single Turkmen
without home.

141
00:15:15,765 --> 00:15:19,845
We'll give villages and tribes
to everyone.

142
00:15:30,765 --> 00:15:35,005
It seems that this won't be enough.

143
00:15:36,505 --> 00:15:39,285
If they are flowing here...

144
00:15:40,605 --> 00:15:42,925
then, we'll march together.

145
00:15:44,045 --> 00:15:48,165
We'll flood into the walls of Bursa.

146
00:15:49,965 --> 00:15:52,345
İznik, Yenişehir.

147
00:15:53,125 --> 00:15:54,925
We'll march altogether.

148
00:15:56,185 --> 00:15:57,725
As long as...

149
00:16:00,265 --> 00:16:05,045
we stand together.

150
00:16:05,585 --> 00:16:09,385
The future of the Turks is on
your hands, Osman Bey.

151
00:16:09,765 --> 00:16:12,705
The reach of the Islam flag...

152
00:16:13,225 --> 00:16:15,285
is in your scope.

153
00:16:16,665 --> 00:16:17,925
Now tell me.

154
00:16:18,945 --> 00:16:20,525
What's your target?

155
00:16:28,215 --> 00:16:29,815
Bursa.

156
00:16:37,185 --> 00:16:43,095
My scope and cause is longer
than my life.

157
00:16:50,585 --> 00:16:56,675
Osman will target Yenişehir after
İnegöl and Bilecik.

158
00:16:59,845 --> 00:17:06,065
If he can take that, you'll be his
right hand for life.

159
00:17:07,335 --> 00:17:09,835
Your dagger won't hurt him.

160
00:17:13,415 --> 00:17:18,105
Do you know my dagger, Romanos?

161
00:17:19,795 --> 00:17:26,165
Or, do you know how far
I can go?

162
00:17:28,425 --> 00:17:33,535
I spent my years behind
Osman that I hate!

163
00:17:34,475 --> 00:17:37,335
I stayed loyal to him.

164
00:17:38,615 --> 00:17:42,245
I've beaten my grudge.

165
00:17:43,715 --> 00:17:47,765
Now tell me.
Who am I?

166
00:17:51,025 --> 00:17:55,495
Barkın. Bey.

167
00:18:00,815 --> 00:18:02,665
Are you afraid of me?

168
00:18:06,875 --> 00:18:10,665
Good. So will Osman.

169
00:18:32,875 --> 00:18:38,425
Back then Osman asked for the villages
around Yenişehir from the emperor.

170
00:18:39,805 --> 00:18:42,395
Now he'll target Yenişehir.

171
00:18:43,015 --> 00:18:46,515
Osman's targets are bigger
than years, Romanos.

172
00:18:46,515 --> 00:18:48,305
What will we do?

173
00:18:48,785 --> 00:18:50,345
Will we stand idle?

174
00:18:50,345 --> 00:18:54,565
You are a commander. You'll
take cautions.

175
00:18:55,845 --> 00:18:59,705
He'll take Yenişehir and make it
his quarters.

176
00:19:00,475 --> 00:19:02,035
Stack soldiers.

177
00:19:03,235 --> 00:19:06,915
Then, he'll target Yondhisar Castle.

178
00:19:07,585 --> 00:19:09,175
Stack soldiers.

179
00:19:09,545 --> 00:19:11,775
Will that be enough to
stop Osman?

180
00:19:12,145 --> 00:19:15,215
Osman is strengthened by
the wind of conquest.

181
00:19:16,375 --> 00:19:18,835
It's difficult to beat him on
the battlefield.

182
00:19:20,085 --> 00:19:25,345
But we'll destroy him.

183
00:19:25,935 --> 00:19:28,405
The war will be over before
it starts.

184
00:19:30,485 --> 00:19:35,895
Come on. Eat our meal.
Get some strength.

185
00:19:36,375 --> 00:19:41,615
Don't fade when you hear
Osman's real target is Bursa.

186
00:19:45,975 --> 00:19:47,865
Bursa is far from you.

187
00:19:48,125 --> 00:19:50,715
Bursa is difficult for you, Osman Bey.

188
00:19:51,565 --> 00:19:54,165
Maybe you shouldn't set seeds
early?

189
00:19:55,845 --> 00:20:00,505
The one with strong roots
can green in the hardest winter.

190
00:20:00,885 --> 00:20:05,775
Surely, it will take years.

191
00:20:06,775 --> 00:20:09,105
But I know one thing.

192
00:20:10,045 --> 00:20:15,135
A mare that gives birth in İnegöl,
will cool down in Bursa's waters.

193
00:20:17,215 --> 00:20:19,245
There is no sooner or later.

194
00:20:20,325 --> 00:20:25,405
There are hard paths and
harder people who walk them.

195
00:20:28,595 --> 00:20:31,205
Your move is ready for the field.
But inside?

196
00:20:31,465 --> 00:20:37,145
If you can't control the flood of Turkmens,
decay from inside will begin.

197
00:20:38,235 --> 00:20:42,795
We host the incoming Turkmens
in Bilecik and İnegöl.

198
00:20:43,735 --> 00:20:49,465
We gave them home but
now it won't be enough.

199
00:20:50,085 --> 00:20:54,005
For that reason, I'll take
another land.

200
00:20:58,235 --> 00:21:02,615
Before Bursa, Yenişehir.

201
00:21:03,825 --> 00:21:05,805
We'll take Yenişehir.

202
00:21:06,115 --> 00:21:11,475
And for Bursa's siege,
we'll make it our quarters.

203
00:21:12,325 --> 00:21:16,105
The flooding Turkmens will
make it home.

204
00:21:16,275 --> 00:21:19,045
We say that your trouble grows
with you.

205
00:21:19,275 --> 00:21:22,225
The bigger trouble is in where
you are heading.

206
00:21:22,665 --> 00:21:26,605
Victories of Bilecik and İnegöl
is boiling Constantinople.

207
00:21:27,205 --> 00:21:29,305
An army is being prepared.

208
00:21:29,685 --> 00:21:33,225
And the Mongols are mobilizing
again.

209
00:21:33,875 --> 00:21:38,385
Turkmens, caravans, villages
are getting raided.

210
00:21:38,845 --> 00:21:41,355
We are ready for all kinds
of troubles.

211
00:21:41,785 --> 00:21:45,625
We sent alps everywhere against
the leaderless Mongols.

212
00:21:46,705 --> 00:21:49,205
They will be killed at sight.

213
00:21:50,455 --> 00:21:52,265
But the army...

214
00:21:54,005 --> 00:21:56,855
we'll take Yenişehir before the
army comes.

215
00:21:57,345 --> 00:22:02,555
If we take Yenişehir, they can face us
with as many soldiers as they want.

216
00:22:04,885 --> 00:22:07,395
The road to Bursa will be open.

217
00:22:18,345 --> 00:22:22,845
May Allah put you in easy circumstances.

218
00:22:23,275 --> 00:22:25,005
May Allah bless your jihad.

219
00:22:25,025 --> 00:22:26,395
Thank you.

220
00:22:26,545 --> 00:22:29,515
Allah's cause is in our heart.

221
00:22:30,145 --> 00:22:37,005
It shows us the way. It makes the
circumstances easier.

222
00:22:38,015 --> 00:22:39,885
May Allah bless your jihad.

223
00:22:40,215 --> 00:22:41,915
Thank you.

224
00:22:42,915 --> 00:22:44,625
Thank you.

225
00:22:55,005 --> 00:22:56,565
Bursa?

226
00:22:57,755 --> 00:23:00,465
-What are you saying?
-Bursa, yes.

227
00:23:01,755 --> 00:23:07,875
If we don't stop Osman, he'll take
Yenişehir and Bursa.

228
00:23:10,245 --> 00:23:12,635
This will ruin your plans too.

229
00:23:14,935 --> 00:23:17,725
Fortunately, the emperor
is preparing a great army.

230
00:23:18,135 --> 00:23:21,435
He should. He should.

231
00:23:22,995 --> 00:23:27,095
I'll send a part of this army to
Yenişehir and Yondhisar.

232
00:23:28,285 --> 00:23:32,705
If it's true, we must form
a good defensive line.

233
00:23:36,295 --> 00:23:38,555
You can't stop Osman by
defending.

234
00:23:40,085 --> 00:23:41,825
We'll attack.

235
00:23:42,465 --> 00:23:44,785
If Osman grew...

236
00:23:45,895 --> 00:23:52,335
we'll take away little tiny parts
from him.

237
00:23:54,565 --> 00:23:59,045
Mind always shows the
same path.

238
00:24:00,775 --> 00:24:03,155
I'm happy so agree with you.

239
00:24:04,975 --> 00:24:06,875
My plan is ready.

240
00:24:08,155 --> 00:24:09,965
My pawn is ready.

241
00:24:10,785 --> 00:24:11,815
Tell me.

242
00:24:12,075 --> 00:24:15,815
There are some leaderless Mongols
who joined the rebellion in Süremiş.

243
00:24:17,095 --> 00:24:18,935
They are out of order.

244
00:24:20,005 --> 00:24:23,715
They need gold to survive.

245
00:24:25,105 --> 00:24:28,205
I'll send them to Osman.

246
00:24:29,475 --> 00:24:34,765
Just as you said. Piece by piece.

247
00:24:36,075 --> 00:24:37,875
You thought well.

248
00:24:38,675 --> 00:24:43,275
But Çobanoğlu Tribe's bey and son...

249
00:24:44,825 --> 00:24:46,915
are going to visit Kayı Tribe.

250
00:24:49,035 --> 00:24:53,265
They respect Ertuğrul Bey
and Osman.

251
00:24:54,255 --> 00:24:56,335
You are giving bad news today.

252
00:24:57,785 --> 00:24:59,855
Let me give you good news then.

253
00:25:00,895 --> 00:25:05,855
Ali's son Mustafa isn't acting
by his own mind.

254
00:25:06,595 --> 00:25:08,875
He acts as his Lala Ahmed says.

255
00:25:09,875 --> 00:25:11,305
What do you think?

256
00:25:11,685 --> 00:25:17,915
Ahmed and I are students of Master
Darius that you don't like.

257
00:25:19,015 --> 00:25:20,645
Ahmed is my friend.

258
00:25:20,685 --> 00:25:25,085
If Ahmed is on our side,
so is Mustafa.

259
00:25:26,525 --> 00:25:30,025
What will we do? Provoke him?

260
00:25:30,615 --> 00:25:33,565
Mustafa isn't the bey yet.
But...

261
00:25:34,125 --> 00:25:40,095
we'll provoke Mustafa so much that
he'll provoke his father Ali.

262
00:25:42,565 --> 00:25:45,115
When Ali Bey differs from Osman...

263
00:25:45,795 --> 00:25:49,505
the beys will be loyal
to Ali Bey.

264
00:25:50,225 --> 00:25:54,935
Then, the war will end before it
starts for Osman.

265
00:25:58,545 --> 00:26:01,295
When the great Roman army
marches...

266
00:26:02,895 --> 00:26:06,625
Osman won't have power left
to fight.

267
00:26:08,345 --> 00:26:10,485
When Osman vanishes...

268
00:26:11,235 --> 00:26:15,225
only one person will stand in
these lands.

269
00:26:21,075 --> 00:26:23,775
İnegöl Castle

270
00:26:36,425 --> 00:26:39,065
-Are they fresh?
-Yes, fresh.

271
00:26:39,555 --> 00:26:41,495
Show me your skills.

272
00:26:43,025 --> 00:26:45,195
Osman Bey is coming!

273
00:26:57,655 --> 00:27:02,305
Welcome, Osman Bey!
Welcome, Osman Bey!

274
00:27:03,255 --> 00:27:08,445
Welcome, Osman Bey!
Welcome, Osman Bey!

275
00:27:08,515 --> 00:27:10,015
Salam Alaikum!

276
00:27:10,395 --> 00:27:13,155
May God protect you, Osman Bey!

277
00:27:13,995 --> 00:27:17,265
Welcome, Osman Bey!

278
00:27:17,575 --> 00:27:19,085
Thank you.

279
00:27:19,165 --> 00:27:21,035
May God make you stronger!

280
00:27:21,225 --> 00:27:23,865
We prospered because of you!

281
00:27:32,085 --> 00:27:34,855
How is the building of the church going,
Priest Hristo?

282
00:27:34,855 --> 00:27:39,215
Our people are working. They don't hold
back their goods or efforts.

283
00:27:39,855 --> 00:27:42,565
Your alps are helping too.
Thank you.

284
00:27:42,915 --> 00:27:48,285
Let's finish it soon. The people's needs
should be provided.

285
00:27:49,465 --> 00:27:54,525
Osman Bey's tent and Turgut Bey's
audience is always open to the people.

286
00:27:55,715 --> 00:27:58,095
May God keep you with us.

287
00:27:58,865 --> 00:28:00,025
Thank you.

288
00:28:04,145 --> 00:28:08,255
-Welcome, Osman Bey.
-Thank you, Turgut Bey.

289
00:28:09,705 --> 00:28:13,095
-How is the tribe?
-We have a big guest.

290
00:28:13,715 --> 00:28:16,285
Çobanoğlu Ali Bey is coming.

291
00:28:16,305 --> 00:28:17,835
The tribe is getting ready.

292
00:28:17,875 --> 00:28:21,455
Ali Bey! He is welcome.

293
00:28:22,735 --> 00:28:26,565
-Come, Osman Bey.
-Thank you.

294
00:28:27,625 --> 00:28:29,215
Thank you.

295
00:28:50,175 --> 00:28:51,715
My sisters!

296
00:28:52,205 --> 00:28:56,705
Let's put in the extra effort!
Çobanoğlu Ali Bey is coming!

297
00:28:57,525 --> 00:28:59,755
And he is coming to congratulate
Osman Bey!

298
00:28:59,945 --> 00:29:03,115
Let's host them to make
Osman Bey proud.

299
00:29:04,095 --> 00:29:09,785
We will! We will! Our women are
capable in fighting and cooking.

300
00:29:13,455 --> 00:29:18,105
Alaca, be careful with the tents
of our guests.

301
00:29:19,065 --> 00:29:22,895
We prepared everything with Zehra.
Everything is done.

302
00:29:23,595 --> 00:29:28,295
Çobanoğlu Ali Bey is coming
to congratulate Osman Bey!

303
00:29:31,275 --> 00:29:32,765
Thank you.

304
00:30:02,215 --> 00:30:07,085
If we get Çobanoğlu Tribe's
support, there will be more conquests.

305
00:30:07,995 --> 00:30:11,245
With Allah's approval,
that support is ready, Malhun Hatun.

306
00:30:11,555 --> 00:30:16,095
Since Ali Bey heard the victory of İnegöl,
he has been talking about Osman Bey.

307
00:30:17,045 --> 00:30:18,545
Thank Allah.

308
00:30:23,095 --> 00:30:25,955
My angelic girl.
Well done.

309
00:30:33,195 --> 00:30:36,205
Bala. Wait.
Let's do it together.

310
00:30:42,315 --> 00:30:45,175
Thank you, Aygül.

311
00:31:00,645 --> 00:31:02,365
I should check.

312
00:31:09,495 --> 00:31:11,215
Ayşe.

313
00:31:14,635 --> 00:31:17,115
It's been a long time since
you last talked.

314
00:31:18,375 --> 00:31:20,175
Is it not the time yet?

315
00:31:46,885 --> 00:31:48,195
Bala!

316
00:31:48,265 --> 00:31:49,355
Bala!

317
00:31:49,375 --> 00:31:50,195
Mother Bala!

318
00:31:50,245 --> 00:31:50,835
Bala!

319
00:31:50,845 --> 00:31:51,865
Bala!

320
00:31:51,915 --> 00:31:52,705
Bala!

321
00:31:52,785 --> 00:31:55,305
Women, bring water!

322
00:31:55,455 --> 00:31:56,475
Bala!

323
00:31:56,485 --> 00:31:57,275
Bala!

324
00:31:58,895 --> 00:32:00,625
She is breathing.

325
00:32:00,635 --> 00:32:01,765
Women!

326
00:32:01,805 --> 00:32:03,555
Come on!

327
00:32:03,655 --> 00:32:05,185
Come on!

328
00:32:17,885 --> 00:32:19,765
Brother! Brother Orhun!

329
00:32:20,145 --> 00:32:22,165
Wait, brother.
What happened?

330
00:32:22,525 --> 00:32:25,385
I was with you a moment ago.
Missed me already?

331
00:32:26,485 --> 00:32:29,585
An evangel, brother.
It's for you.

332
00:32:30,175 --> 00:32:31,735
From Holafira.

333
00:32:34,935 --> 00:32:39,695
But I want to use your dagger that
you don't let me touch.

334
00:32:41,155 --> 00:32:43,965
Sure, brother.
Sure.

335
00:32:47,235 --> 00:32:48,795
Brother.

336
00:32:49,965 --> 00:32:52,465
My dear brother.
Take it.

337
00:33:08,615 --> 00:33:10,955
What does it say?
Is she alright?

338
00:33:11,035 --> 00:33:12,815
Did she arrive safely?

339
00:33:12,835 --> 00:33:14,595
She is alright.

340
00:33:15,195 --> 00:33:17,055
Her aunt is taking good
care of her.

341
00:33:17,055 --> 00:33:19,055
Everything is as she wants.

342
00:33:21,735 --> 00:33:24,315
She already missed our tribe a lot.

343
00:33:26,415 --> 00:33:28,975
She says that she'll come back
one day.

344
00:33:30,155 --> 00:33:32,715
Inshallah, brother.
Inshallah.

345
00:33:44,255 --> 00:33:46,835
If İnegöl is a lake...

346
00:33:48,695 --> 00:33:50,715
Bursa is a sea.

347
00:33:52,515 --> 00:33:55,035
It won't be easy to take it.

348
00:33:56,735 --> 00:33:59,595
Sieging Bursa and İznik...

349
00:34:00,755 --> 00:34:02,835
might take years.

350
00:34:04,615 --> 00:34:06,135
Firstly...

351
00:34:06,875 --> 00:34:09,435
we'll get the caravan routes.

352
00:34:09,435 --> 00:34:11,995
We'll cut their veins.

353
00:34:12,034 --> 00:34:15,574
We'll spot the sources of
the city and take them over.

354
00:34:16,614 --> 00:34:20,355
Their mines, farms and everthing.

355
00:34:21,335 --> 00:34:24,074
This will be our move against them.

356
00:34:26,135 --> 00:34:28,635
The emperor is building an
army against us.

357
00:34:29,695 --> 00:34:33,935
His intention is to take us out of
these lands.

358
00:34:36,915 --> 00:34:39,495
-Let them come, my bey.
-No.

359
00:34:40,955 --> 00:34:43,735
The real bravery is needed soon.

360
00:34:46,695 --> 00:34:49,235
We have only one arrow to shoot.

361
00:34:54,554 --> 00:34:56,114
Yenişehir.

362
00:35:00,255 --> 00:35:01,775
We'll position there.

363
00:35:02,195 --> 00:35:04,295
And we'll defend it.

364
00:35:06,295 --> 00:35:09,435
If we can't stop the incoming
army...

365
00:35:10,075 --> 00:35:13,575
İnegöl that we took with the lives
of many martyrs and my brother...

366
00:35:14,615 --> 00:35:16,395
will be taken away.

367
00:35:19,795 --> 00:35:21,815
If we start retreating...

368
00:35:22,655 --> 00:35:24,015
then...

369
00:35:25,035 --> 00:35:27,595
we might have to retreat to
the Kayı Tribe.

370
00:35:32,255 --> 00:35:34,755
So, there is no place
for mistakes.

371
00:35:36,375 --> 00:35:39,475
Precautions or war.

372
00:35:39,895 --> 00:35:41,755
We'll do anything, Osman Bey.

373
00:35:42,495 --> 00:35:45,055
But what will we do to the leaderless
Mongols?

374
00:35:45,575 --> 00:35:50,355
They are troubling the
caravans and the villagers.

375
00:35:50,795 --> 00:35:54,855
So, the trouble continues in the
east and in the west.

376
00:35:55,835 --> 00:35:59,635
Cerkutay and Konur are tracing them.

377
00:36:00,375 --> 00:36:02,415
They'll take care of them.

378
00:36:03,755 --> 00:36:05,295
Thank you, my bey.

379
00:36:05,735 --> 00:36:07,775
-Master Davud.
-My bey.

380
00:36:08,375 --> 00:36:11,555
You'll go to Yenişehir with
Kumral Abdal.

381
00:36:12,735 --> 00:36:16,575
Get capable masters with you.
Dervishes with smooth tongues.

382
00:36:16,795 --> 00:36:18,155
Firstly...

383
00:36:19,255 --> 00:36:21,395
firstly, you'll conquer
the hearts.

384
00:36:22,335 --> 00:36:24,835
Priest Hristo will come with you.

385
00:36:24,875 --> 00:36:26,635
As you order, my bey.

386
00:36:27,775 --> 00:36:32,315
We can conquer any heart
with the light of our Allah.

387
00:36:33,635 --> 00:36:35,955
We'll go and take them.

388
00:36:36,095 --> 00:36:37,635
Thank Allah.

389
00:36:37,875 --> 00:36:40,055
Our target is the order of the world.

390
00:36:40,975 --> 00:36:45,775
But the Kayı can't do it
alone.

391
00:36:48,115 --> 00:36:51,675
Çobanoğlu Ali Bey will visit us.

392
00:36:51,935 --> 00:36:53,655
He is a great bey.

393
00:36:54,115 --> 00:36:56,155
And it requires a great
preparation.

394
00:36:56,375 --> 00:36:59,815
He'll be hosted as he deserves it.
You see it fit.

395
00:37:00,015 --> 00:37:03,395
Come on, then. Everyone to
their jobs.

396
00:37:04,455 --> 00:37:06,495
May our jihad be blessed.

397
00:37:36,235 --> 00:37:37,795
Thank you.

398
00:37:40,685 --> 00:37:42,565
Thank you, mother.

399
00:37:52,085 --> 00:37:53,925
All those years...

400
00:37:55,005 --> 00:37:57,065
I've waited to reunite with you.

401
00:37:58,265 --> 00:38:00,805
I lost my father as soon
as I reunited with him!

402
00:38:01,785 --> 00:38:04,365
Do you want me to not reunite
with you either, mother?

403
00:38:05,445 --> 00:38:06,745
Always...

404
00:38:07,665 --> 00:38:10,665
I dreamed of sitting around a table
altogether.

405
00:38:12,665 --> 00:38:14,405
Now I'm with you.

406
00:38:14,445 --> 00:38:17,725
I'm in my tribe, my home now!

407
00:38:18,245 --> 00:38:20,445
But now you keep your voice
away from me!

408
00:38:23,665 --> 00:38:25,705
What is this for, mother?

409
00:38:25,845 --> 00:38:27,165
Didn't you...

410
00:38:28,045 --> 00:38:31,405
tell me that I'm a martyr's son
and I should stand tall?

411
00:38:31,585 --> 00:38:33,165
Look at me!

412
00:38:33,745 --> 00:38:36,605
I stand tall and proud of
my father.

413
00:38:36,825 --> 00:38:38,605
What about you, mother?

414
00:38:39,085 --> 00:38:41,085
Why are you silent?

415
00:38:42,105 --> 00:38:44,645
You don't drop a single tear.

416
00:38:45,965 --> 00:38:47,845
What about your heart?

417
00:39:07,205 --> 00:39:11,065
Is it only your bey
who is a martyr?

418
00:39:12,285 --> 00:39:15,285
My father died!
Father!

419
00:39:17,365 --> 00:39:19,905
When my only medicine is
your voice...

420
00:39:22,525 --> 00:39:24,405
you kept it away from me.

421
00:39:30,925 --> 00:39:33,435
I'll make you speak, mother!

422
00:39:33,905 --> 00:39:35,745
You will speak, mother!

423
00:39:37,425 --> 00:39:39,145
Come on!

424
00:39:40,185 --> 00:39:42,005
Come on, you too!

425
00:39:51,905 --> 00:39:53,905
Is this how you face the enemy?

426
00:39:54,285 --> 00:39:55,585
Come on!

427
00:40:46,845 --> 00:40:48,685
Won't you talk, mother?

428
00:40:50,665 --> 00:40:52,445
When will you talk?

429
00:40:53,585 --> 00:40:56,145
When my burial comes to the tribe?

430
00:40:58,325 --> 00:41:01,445
Alps! Come on! To Osman Bey!

431
00:41:23,625 --> 00:41:24,945
Look...

432
00:41:30,485 --> 00:41:32,985
I am telling you, Romanos...

433
00:41:33,165 --> 00:41:37,745
...we were both trained by Master Arius.

434
00:41:39,905 --> 00:41:42,465
That dagger on my throat is ours.

435
00:41:49,485 --> 00:41:52,025
Barkın, my dear friend!

436
00:41:56,565 --> 00:41:58,285
You get old but...

437
00:41:58,705 --> 00:42:00,765
...you never lose your skills.

438
00:42:01,725 --> 00:42:04,305
I didn't even hear a crackle.

439
00:42:04,365 --> 00:42:06,125
This is how people are.

440
00:42:06,305 --> 00:42:10,125
They forget their names but don't forget
their training.

441
00:42:12,245 --> 00:42:15,765
If you have raised Mustafa, son of
Çobanoğlu Ali Bey like this...

442
00:42:16,805 --> 00:42:19,365
...it means he is as dangerous as you.

443
00:42:19,405 --> 00:42:20,985
Mustafa.

444
00:42:21,465 --> 00:42:24,885
Anger runs in his veins, not blood.

445
00:42:25,665 --> 00:42:30,905
It is very easy to dominate such a person
and to raise him as you wish.

446
00:42:32,105 --> 00:42:33,865
Tell me, Ahmet.

447
00:42:34,745 --> 00:42:36,325
Tell me more.

448
00:42:36,385 --> 00:42:39,385
His father Ata Bey's calmness drives him
crazy.

449
00:42:39,485 --> 00:42:41,025
His blood boils.

450
00:42:41,085 --> 00:42:44,565
He is also the angriest at the fact that
he left those conquests to Kayı.

451
00:42:45,905 --> 00:42:48,485
So, he is perfect for our game?

452
00:42:48,585 --> 00:42:51,665
He would drown Osman in a spoon of water
if he could.

453
00:42:54,725 --> 00:42:56,825
He is a very furious young man.

454
00:42:57,465 --> 00:42:59,345
I will force this side of him.

455
00:43:00,465 --> 00:43:02,345
If I can provoke Mustafa...

456
00:43:02,705 --> 00:43:04,565
...he might convince his father.

457
00:43:09,065 --> 00:43:10,585
Good.

458
00:43:12,285 --> 00:43:13,805
Osman will turn into ash...

459
00:43:14,625 --> 00:43:20,645
...between a strong Turk Tribe and
the strong army of Rome.

460
00:43:22,445 --> 00:43:24,965
And the cleverest, the fiercest man...

461
00:43:25,565 --> 00:43:28,075
...will start this fire.

462
00:43:33,225 --> 00:43:35,505
Indeed, it has already begun.

463
00:43:50,885 --> 00:43:52,935
What is going on here?

464
00:44:08,905 --> 00:44:10,665
What is going on here?

465
00:44:17,605 --> 00:44:18,905
No.

466
00:44:19,225 --> 00:44:20,805
Don't be afraid.

467
00:44:20,885 --> 00:44:22,385
Don't be afraid.

468
00:44:24,025 --> 00:44:25,865
Come here.

469
00:44:36,585 --> 00:44:38,465
What happened here?

470
00:44:38,465 --> 00:44:40,245
Who did this?

471
00:44:40,285 --> 00:44:43,585
The evil Mongols stopped us on our way.

472
00:44:44,285 --> 00:44:46,165
They raided our goods.

473
00:44:47,745 --> 00:44:50,445
Come here. Come here.

474
00:44:55,725 --> 00:44:59,265
Why did they let you live?

475
00:45:00,725 --> 00:45:05,585
These devil Mongols never let anyone live
after their raids.

476
00:45:06,065 --> 00:45:07,885
Your alps, Osman Bey.

477
00:45:07,885 --> 00:45:09,705
They came just in time.

478
00:45:09,705 --> 00:45:11,955
We would already be dead if it weren't
for them.

479
00:45:12,185 --> 00:45:14,765
The Mongols ran this way when they saw
them.

480
00:45:15,485 --> 00:45:17,345
Your alps went after them.

481
00:45:19,145 --> 00:45:20,985
Let's go after them.

482
00:45:21,645 --> 00:45:23,145
As you order, my Bey.

483
00:45:24,945 --> 00:45:26,705
Let's go, my Bey.

484
00:45:26,745 --> 00:45:29,785
Let them know what they get for hurting
the innocent.

485
00:45:30,085 --> 00:45:33,185
Of course.

486
00:45:37,765 --> 00:45:39,825
What happened, Cerkutay?

487
00:45:40,925 --> 00:45:43,025
I found some Mongol tracks.

488
00:45:43,185 --> 00:45:45,225
I knew something was wrong.

489
00:45:45,445 --> 00:45:47,965
The tracks led us to here, my Bey.

490
00:45:53,265 --> 00:45:54,965
Were they crowded?

491
00:45:54,965 --> 00:45:56,985
Ten or fifteen, my Bey.

492
00:45:57,005 --> 00:45:59,085
They took the goods and ran away.

493
00:45:59,175 --> 00:46:01,515
We killed all of them and didn't leave...

494
00:46:01,565 --> 00:46:04,145
...a single good of these merchants
to them.

495
00:46:05,985 --> 00:46:09,085
Share these goods among the people.

496
00:46:09,425 --> 00:46:12,245
Indemnify the damages.

497
00:46:12,505 --> 00:46:14,725
Take the wounded to the healing tent.

498
00:46:14,725 --> 00:46:16,265
As you order, my Bey.

499
00:46:16,265 --> 00:46:18,785
Thank you, Osman Bey. May God protect
you.

500
00:46:19,045 --> 00:46:20,585
Don't worry.

501
00:46:21,325 --> 00:46:24,405
No one under my rule will be mistreated.

502
00:46:25,585 --> 00:46:27,605
Whoever harms my people, punishing
him...

503
00:46:27,985 --> 00:46:30,695
...is my holy duty.

504
00:46:32,035 --> 00:46:36,235
Even if people's noses bleed, I will ask
for their account now.

505
00:46:36,235 --> 00:46:37,785
Don't worry.

506
00:46:37,785 --> 00:46:39,785
We are grateful, Osman Bey.

507
00:46:42,265 --> 00:46:45,495
So, these dogs have settled around.

508
00:46:46,895 --> 00:46:50,935
Konur, you will join Turgut Bey with
Aktemur.

509
00:46:51,035 --> 00:46:52,625
As you order, my Bey.

510
00:46:52,735 --> 00:46:54,265
Cerkutay.

511
00:46:54,285 --> 00:46:55,825
Yes, my Bey?

512
00:46:55,835 --> 00:46:57,905
Go after these Mongols.

513
00:46:58,635 --> 00:47:00,205
As you order, my Bey.

514
00:47:02,325 --> 00:47:04,895
I will destroy their dens.

515
00:47:22,005 --> 00:47:24,085
Her face looks very pale.

516
00:47:25,045 --> 00:47:28,955
She has been working since morning prayer.
I told her not to but she didn't listen.

517
00:47:32,155 --> 00:47:35,005
She fell to the ground just like that.
I was so worried.

518
00:47:36,525 --> 00:47:38,355
Ah, Bala, Ah.

519
00:47:42,895 --> 00:47:45,895
She will be fine, right, Healer Sister?

520
00:47:46,785 --> 00:47:50,125
She got weakened, but she will regain her
strength by drinking this.

521
00:47:50,955 --> 00:47:54,495
-I hope so.
-I hope so.

522
00:47:57,605 --> 00:47:59,165
Mother!

523
00:48:06,385 --> 00:48:08,885
Is my mother fine? Did she get ill?

524
00:48:08,885 --> 00:48:11,405
She is fine and she will be better, son.

525
00:48:11,405 --> 00:48:12,935
She caught a little cold.

526
00:48:12,935 --> 00:48:15,495
Let's leave and let her rest.

527
00:48:19,985 --> 00:48:21,495
Zehra.

528
00:48:21,695 --> 00:48:23,155
You stay with her.

529
00:48:23,155 --> 00:48:24,525
Call me if anything happens.

530
00:48:24,525 --> 00:48:26,525
Don't worry.

531
00:48:28,750 --> 00:48:30,840
What does Healer Hatun say?

532
00:48:31,520 --> 00:48:33,060
I should stay with her.

533
00:48:33,060 --> 00:48:35,060
She may need something.

534
00:48:35,640 --> 00:48:39,150
Healer Hatun says that your mother is a
little tired, my Alaaddin.

535
00:48:39,150 --> 00:48:40,460
But she is fine.

536
00:48:41,520 --> 00:48:43,690
Don't worry, my Alaaddin.
Healer Sister is...

537
00:48:43,690 --> 00:48:46,520
...with her. Don't be afraid.

538
00:48:47,180 --> 00:48:48,500
Let's go...

539
00:48:48,500 --> 00:48:50,440
...and let Bala sleep.

540
00:48:52,920 --> 00:48:54,480
Come on.

541
00:48:59,340 --> 00:49:01,910
Roadside Caravanserai

542
00:49:04,585 --> 00:49:06,665
In the name of Allah.

543
00:49:11,305 --> 00:49:14,845
Osman Bey welcomes us on the way.

544
00:49:15,905 --> 00:49:18,445
Are the roads not safe, Turgut Bey?

545
00:49:18,555 --> 00:49:21,085
The roads are never safe in this area.

546
00:49:21,505 --> 00:49:24,075
But only if we are not there.

547
00:49:25,985 --> 00:49:28,745
We clear the roads from any looters.

548
00:49:29,445 --> 00:49:31,535
Thank you. Thank you.

549
00:49:34,385 --> 00:49:37,045
Your visit also honored us, Ali Bey.

550
00:49:37,475 --> 00:49:41,215
Welcoming a Mighty Turk Bey like you
is an honor for us.

551
00:49:41,385 --> 00:49:42,645
Don't worry.

552
00:49:42,645 --> 00:49:45,715
Your caravan on the way will be
accompanied to Söğüt.

553
00:49:46,155 --> 00:49:48,245
It is under our protection.

554
00:49:48,735 --> 00:49:52,955
The real honor is to sit at this table
with you, Turgut Bey.

555
00:49:56,075 --> 00:49:58,105
All right.

556
00:49:59,275 --> 00:50:00,845
The real honor is...

557
00:50:00,905 --> 00:50:02,415
...war!

558
00:50:02,955 --> 00:50:06,755
Come on, continue to tell from where you
left off.

559
00:50:06,955 --> 00:50:11,515
You entered İnegöl with the ram head
while pouring boiling oil from your head.

560
00:50:12,305 --> 00:50:13,875
What happened after that?

561
00:50:14,815 --> 00:50:16,345
Later...

562
00:50:16,435 --> 00:50:17,945
...our skilled valiants...

563
00:50:18,105 --> 00:50:19,675
...Osman Bey...

564
00:50:20,015 --> 00:50:25,575
...and brother Gündüz, who was a martyr,
risking his life to take İnegöl.

565
00:50:26,815 --> 00:50:28,575
And many other alps.

566
00:50:28,575 --> 00:50:30,105
Thanks to them.

567
00:50:30,105 --> 00:50:32,685
Yes, we took over the castle...

568
00:50:32,845 --> 00:50:37,405
... but we took every step with our blood
and soul.

569
00:50:40,185 --> 00:50:44,775
I've heard about both Gündüz Bey and
his heroism, Aktemur.

570
00:50:46,245 --> 00:50:49,835
Your father became a son befitting
his ancestors.

571
00:50:50,615 --> 00:50:52,445
May he rest in peace.

572
00:50:54,705 --> 00:50:56,585
Thank you, Ali Bey.

573
00:51:02,135 --> 00:51:07,645
I actually wonder about the Emperor's face
when he took Nikola's head.

574
00:51:12,535 --> 00:51:15,355
Aren't you afraid of the Emperor's wrath?

575
00:51:16,135 --> 00:51:18,185
Is this a smart move?

576
00:51:24,335 --> 00:51:27,885
Osman Bey and those who support him
do not have fear in their hearts.

577
00:51:28,535 --> 00:51:30,285
But they scare others.

578
00:51:33,215 --> 00:51:35,985
We sent Nikola's head to our opponents...

579
00:51:36,215 --> 00:51:38,245
... as an example.

580
00:51:39,755 --> 00:51:42,335
There is no conquest with fear.

581
00:51:45,705 --> 00:51:48,205
There is no conquest with fear.

582
00:51:49,075 --> 00:51:51,075
Praise be to you!

583
00:51:51,215 --> 00:51:54,475
Fear is for cowards.

584
00:51:54,475 --> 00:51:56,475
The Turks don't fear.

585
00:51:57,415 --> 00:52:00,615
I understood where Osman Bey's power
came from.

586
00:52:01,445 --> 00:52:08,505
From the valiant men who lined up behind
him and believed in him and his cause.

587
00:52:09,635 --> 00:52:13,215
One who leans his back on the mountains...

588
00:52:13,215 --> 00:52:16,745
...makes his range endless.

589
00:52:18,675 --> 00:52:20,215
Thank you.

590
00:52:20,505 --> 00:52:23,305
Osman Bey's power comes from his cause.

591
00:52:24,075 --> 00:52:28,245
And those who have the same cause
support him.

592
00:52:28,615 --> 00:52:31,155
Thank you, Ali Bey.

593
00:52:33,385 --> 00:52:34,945
Thank you.

594
00:53:11,585 --> 00:53:12,815
Father?

595
00:53:12,815 --> 00:53:15,325
-Welcome, my Bey.
-Welcome, Osman Bey.

596
00:53:16,655 --> 00:53:22,235
Welcome, my Bey.

597
00:53:30,085 --> 00:53:31,615
Father!

598
00:53:32,795 --> 00:53:34,345
Fatma!

599
00:53:38,025 --> 00:53:40,525
My little sheep.

600
00:53:51,085 --> 00:53:52,585
Come here.

601
00:53:53,255 --> 00:53:54,825
Come here.

602
00:53:57,965 --> 00:53:59,555
Sons.

603
00:54:03,145 --> 00:54:04,695
Alaaddin.

604
00:54:07,965 --> 00:54:11,765
Are you upset with each other?

605
00:54:17,640 --> 00:54:20,410
Bala mother is ill, father.

606
00:54:24,130 --> 00:54:25,660
Alaaddin.

607
00:54:27,190 --> 00:54:29,190
Tell me, what happened to your mother?

608
00:54:29,470 --> 00:54:31,970
My mother is in the tent, father.

609
00:54:33,240 --> 00:54:35,300
She doesn't look good.

610
00:54:38,640 --> 00:54:40,730
She passed out in the kitchen.

611
00:54:41,010 --> 00:54:43,040
My mother is with her.

612
00:54:43,530 --> 00:54:45,030
Is that so?

613
00:54:49,130 --> 00:54:52,360
Let me see her. Wait here.

614
00:55:02,240 --> 00:55:03,940
Don't be afraid, brother.

615
00:55:04,530 --> 00:55:06,530
Nothing will happen to our mother.

616
00:55:06,990 --> 00:55:08,830
I hope so, brother.

617
00:55:09,990 --> 00:55:11,740
I hope so.

618
00:55:20,900 --> 00:55:22,410
Malhun...

619
00:55:23,100 --> 00:55:24,600
...how is Bala?

620
00:55:24,600 --> 00:55:27,270
She doesn't feel good, Osman. The healer
is with her.

621
00:55:27,360 --> 00:55:29,140
She will be fine soon.

622
00:55:29,210 --> 00:55:31,600
She worked so much.

623
00:55:31,670 --> 00:55:34,460
She also tired herself in the kitchen
today for the guests.

624
00:55:35,040 --> 00:55:36,930
That must be the reason.

625
00:55:37,540 --> 00:55:39,240
I informed our Sheik.

626
00:55:39,240 --> 00:55:40,740
He will be here in the evening.

627
00:55:40,740 --> 00:55:43,240
He will surely heal Bala with his prayer.

628
00:55:43,610 --> 00:55:45,690
I hope so. I hope so.

629
00:55:47,190 --> 00:55:48,760
Let me see her.

630
00:56:19,085 --> 00:56:20,855
She just fell asleep, my Bey.

631
00:56:20,915 --> 00:56:22,655
But if you please...

632
00:56:22,655 --> 00:56:25,155
...you can see her.

633
00:56:25,695 --> 00:56:27,495
No, let her sleep.

634
00:56:27,695 --> 00:56:29,495
I won't wake her up.

635
00:56:30,525 --> 00:56:32,265
She must rest.

636
00:56:37,525 --> 00:56:39,815
Inform me if anything happens.

637
00:56:58,865 --> 00:57:00,365
Sons.

638
00:57:00,525 --> 00:57:03,045
Father, how is my mother?

639
00:57:04,445 --> 00:57:06,015
Don't worry.

640
00:57:06,675 --> 00:57:09,645
Your mother is fine and she will be
better.

641
00:57:11,045 --> 00:57:12,955
I told you. Bala mother is strong.

642
00:57:12,955 --> 00:57:15,265
Nothing will happen to her.

643
00:57:15,875 --> 00:57:17,745
She is the leader of the women
warriors.

644
00:57:18,675 --> 00:57:20,375
I hope so, brother.

645
00:57:20,675 --> 00:57:22,225
Yes, she is.

646
00:57:22,365 --> 00:57:24,565
She is strong.

647
00:57:25,075 --> 00:57:27,225
But she can't even open her eyes.

648
00:57:27,565 --> 00:57:29,715
I am afraid that something will happen
to her.

649
00:57:29,715 --> 00:57:31,225
No way.

650
00:57:33,105 --> 00:57:34,805
We are all human.

651
00:57:35,645 --> 00:57:37,495
Mothers get tired sometimes as well.

652
00:57:37,535 --> 00:57:39,395
Mothers get ill sometimes as well.

653
00:57:40,145 --> 00:57:47,505
But you will see. She will wake up as if
nothing happened.

654
00:57:47,505 --> 00:57:50,065
And she will stand behind us like
a mountain.

655
00:57:50,775 --> 00:57:54,795
She will rise from the ashes like a
phoenix.

656
00:57:56,335 --> 00:58:01,075
As long as mothers have children who
pray for them like you...

657
00:58:01,505 --> 00:58:03,535
...nothing will happen to them.

658
00:58:10,075 --> 00:58:12,535
The mothers take their strength from their
children.

659
00:58:17,675 --> 00:58:19,425
Come here.

660
00:58:22,625 --> 00:58:25,125
Father, we took Bilecik and İnegöl.

661
00:58:26,625 --> 00:58:28,135
Yes, we did.

662
00:58:28,175 --> 00:58:29,765
Thankfully.

663
00:58:29,845 --> 00:58:32,405
Thankfully. But what about Bursa?

664
00:58:32,405 --> 00:58:34,275
When will we take Bursa?

665
00:58:34,275 --> 00:58:36,275
When will we go there?

666
00:58:39,335 --> 00:58:44,625
Taking Bursa isn't that easy, my Orhan.

667
00:58:45,605 --> 00:58:47,335
Where did this come from?

668
00:58:47,335 --> 00:58:49,335
He keeps talking about it.

669
00:58:49,335 --> 00:58:52,225
My brother dreams of standing on the walls
of Bursa.

670
00:58:52,835 --> 00:58:54,365
Praise be!

671
00:58:54,445 --> 00:58:58,005
If we take Bursa, the infidels will have
no power in the east.

672
00:58:58,135 --> 00:58:59,725
They will be weakened.

673
00:58:59,825 --> 00:59:02,595
This will open the way for many other
conquests, father.

674
00:59:03,475 --> 00:59:07,365
When we take Bursa, our trade will
prosper.

675
00:59:07,425 --> 00:59:09,365
Caravans will never stop.

676
00:59:09,365 --> 00:59:12,125
Because the Constantinople's trade will
be depending on us.

677
00:59:12,125 --> 00:59:14,075
Praise be to my valiants!

678
00:59:15,595 --> 00:59:17,145
Good for you.

679
00:59:18,365 --> 00:59:19,925
Good for you.

680
00:59:21,965 --> 00:59:24,105
From now on...

681
00:59:24,475 --> 00:59:26,305
...our target is Bursa.

682
00:59:28,705 --> 00:59:30,225
Come on.

683
00:59:32,640 --> 00:59:36,220
I wasn't there in İnegöl but I want to
fight beside you in Bursa, father.

684
00:59:38,070 --> 00:59:39,850
I hope so, son.

685
00:59:40,120 --> 00:59:42,892
I hope those days are soon.

686
00:59:48,800 --> 00:59:51,300
Roadside Caravanserai

687
00:59:55,740 --> 00:59:58,480
Despite all the mess in the far away...

688
00:59:58,540 --> 01:00:01,090
...you did a great job, Turgut Bey.

689
01:00:01,110 --> 01:00:04,930
You have won victories beyond your
strength and numbers.

690
01:00:05,620 --> 01:00:07,640
Isn't that the real skill?

691
01:00:08,340 --> 01:00:12,130
Even though you are few, you make more
with your heart.

692
01:00:15,590 --> 01:00:17,660
But I don't understand you Konuralp.

693
01:00:18,380 --> 01:00:22,280
You were the commander of Mighty Seljuk
and now you are the alp to a Bey.

694
01:00:23,460 --> 01:00:27,050
Brag about conquering a castle while you
used to rule cities.

695
01:00:34,500 --> 01:00:37,080
This must be going down in the world.

696
01:00:44,380 --> 01:00:46,960
Hear yourself, Mustafa Bey.

697
01:00:49,420 --> 01:00:53,250
We are supporting Osman Bey for the cause
of Allah--

698
01:00:53,250 --> 01:00:57,790
They say it's better to be a head to
a calf than a foot to an ox.

699
01:00:59,970 --> 01:01:02,710
You are doing that, right?

700
01:01:06,650 --> 01:01:10,240
In the state, your opponent was abundant
and your position was weak.

701
01:01:11,000 --> 01:01:14,000
Now you are a rich man beside Osman Bey.

702
01:01:17,820 --> 01:01:20,640
They have no money, my Bey.

703
01:01:21,080 --> 01:01:25,620
They keep spending what they stole
or plundered from the Sultan.

704
01:01:27,400 --> 01:01:28,980
Aktemur!

705
01:01:29,720 --> 01:01:32,290
Hear yourself!

706
01:01:34,960 --> 01:01:38,810
If not, you don't need to hear at all!

707
01:01:45,760 --> 01:01:48,280
We wanted to host you since you were
our guests.

708
01:01:49,360 --> 01:01:53,410
But you are not our guest anymore due to
your senseless talks.

709
01:01:55,560 --> 01:01:57,420
Get hold of your alps!

710
01:02:01,720 --> 01:02:06,870
We won't listen to those who slander the
people that died for the Turk nation!

711
01:02:10,470 --> 01:02:12,500
If you don't punish him, we know how to
do.

712
01:02:14,950 --> 01:02:17,040
There is no need, right?

713
01:02:35,460 --> 01:02:38,990
I will kill all of you! Devils!

714
01:02:40,800 --> 01:02:45,360
Those who are angry with two sentences
are trying to establish a state.

715
01:02:46,610 --> 01:02:49,460
What do you expect from people living
in tents...

716
01:02:49,570 --> 01:02:52,400
... after winning so many victories
and castles?

717
01:02:52,780 --> 01:02:56,340
Don't cross the line!

718
01:02:57,490 --> 01:02:59,730
It won't be our fault if you keep talking!

719
01:03:01,590 --> 01:03:03,450
Come on, talk!

720
01:03:08,300 --> 01:03:10,160
What is going on here?

721
01:03:11,690 --> 01:03:13,270
Ahmet!

722
01:03:14,760 --> 01:03:18,320
Mustafa, Turgut Bey, stop!

723
01:03:19,880 --> 01:03:21,600
They wounded my alp!

724
01:03:23,760 --> 01:03:26,800
Father, is this going to
remain unpenalized?

725
01:03:34,280 --> 01:03:36,860
Your Alp exceeded his limits, Ali Bey.

726
01:03:38,010 --> 01:03:42,600
He tried to attack once he was forgiven.

727
01:03:48,540 --> 01:03:50,080
Ali Bey!

728
01:03:50,090 --> 01:03:52,660
We kept silent until now because
but now...

729
01:04:12,510 --> 01:04:15,600
What is your duty, Ahmet?

730
01:04:17,190 --> 01:04:20,560
Serving as a model for Mustafa.

731
01:04:20,920 --> 01:04:28,030
Is your duty to make a scene in where
we are guests?

732
01:04:28,060 --> 01:04:29,270
My Bey.

733
01:04:29,270 --> 01:04:31,020
No need for explanation.

734
01:04:32,120 --> 01:04:34,160
Things are obvious.

735
01:04:37,170 --> 01:04:42,980
Neither Turgut Bey nor Konur Alp
holds their sword.

736
01:04:44,210 --> 01:04:48,920
But your swords are ready to swing!

737
01:04:56,130 --> 01:05:00,840
Sorry for the inconvenience, Ali Bey.
We wouldn't want to host you like that.

738
01:05:13,850 --> 01:05:15,810
Well done, Turgut Bey.

739
01:05:17,990 --> 01:05:22,140
Whoever talks against the ones
whose intentions are clear...

740
01:05:23,080 --> 01:05:25,510
...shall confront me.

741
01:05:31,730 --> 01:05:36,780
So as to support Osman Bey
I came to this land!

742
01:05:41,190 --> 01:05:44,990
He is the only hope of Turks!

743
01:05:46,810 --> 01:05:50,330
If I see such vulgarity again...

744
01:05:50,800 --> 01:05:58,370
even if it's my son or friend,
I won't be merciful!

745
01:06:39,010 --> 01:06:40,570
Bala.

746
01:06:42,785 --> 01:06:46,625
If wind touches your hair,
my heart gets cold.

747
01:06:47,025 --> 01:06:50,775
Open your eyes.
Open your eyes.

748
01:06:54,305 --> 01:06:57,275
Osman weakens when he
sees you like this.

749
01:06:58,915 --> 01:07:01,905
Give me strength, Bala.

750
01:07:03,755 --> 01:07:07,685
Bala. Open your eyes.

751
01:07:16,485 --> 01:07:17,995
Bala!

752
01:07:20,775 --> 01:07:22,275
Osman!

753
01:07:22,445 --> 01:07:26,455
Are you alright?
Come, come, come.

754
01:07:29,905 --> 01:07:31,935
What happened to you?

755
01:07:32,525 --> 01:07:35,765
The healer says it's fine.
I'm alright.

756
01:07:36,205 --> 01:07:38,775
Are you tiring yourself too much?

757
01:07:38,795 --> 01:07:40,545
I heard it from Aygül.

758
01:07:40,965 --> 01:07:43,035
You got bad at the soup kitchen.

759
01:07:49,795 --> 01:07:51,355
Bala.

760
01:07:54,685 --> 01:07:58,265
You are smiling.
What is this?

761
01:08:03,565 --> 01:08:05,735
-Osman.
-Yes?

762
01:08:06,955 --> 01:08:08,925
I was suspicious but...

763
01:08:12,645 --> 01:08:14,915
I got sure after seeing
the healer...

764
01:08:16,615 --> 01:08:18,145
What is it?

765
01:08:20,915 --> 01:08:22,955
You'll have another child, Osman.

766
01:08:23,555 --> 01:08:25,055
A baby!

767
01:08:26,154 --> 01:08:28,005
What are you saying?

768
01:08:30,104 --> 01:08:31,615
Really?

769
01:08:34,774 --> 01:08:36,325
Mashallah!

770
01:08:36,654 --> 01:08:41,165
Mashallah! Mashallah!
Thank Allah!

771
01:08:41,385 --> 01:08:45,104
Thank Allah, Bala!

772
01:08:45,365 --> 01:08:46,925
Bala!

773
01:08:52,015 --> 01:08:53,725
Thank Allah!

774
01:08:55,495 --> 01:08:57,015
Bala!

775
01:08:58,185 --> 01:08:59,715
My love!

776
01:09:00,274 --> 01:09:01,814
My phoenix!

777
01:09:04,785 --> 01:09:11,024
Our family is growing,
expanding!

778
01:09:13,165 --> 01:09:14,944
Thank Allah!

779
01:09:16,484 --> 01:09:18,194
Thank Allah!

780
01:09:31,145 --> 01:09:32,845
How is my mother?

781
01:09:33,854 --> 01:09:35,725
I can't eat anything.

782
01:09:41,505 --> 01:09:44,055
Be at ease, my shehzad.

783
01:09:44,685 --> 01:09:48,234
There is good in what
seems to be bad.

784
01:09:50,265 --> 01:09:53,814
Your mother will be fine.
Just pray.

785
01:09:55,015 --> 01:09:56,835
I always pray.

786
01:09:57,785 --> 01:10:02,285
I always pray for mother
from inside.

787
01:10:04,555 --> 01:10:06,655
Mashallah to you.

788
01:10:23,425 --> 01:10:26,785
Father. Isn't my mother coming?

789
01:10:28,495 --> 01:10:31,755
Sit, Alahaddin.
Sit.

790
01:10:44,765 --> 01:10:48,565
Your mother is fine.
She'll be better, inshallah.

791
01:10:49,835 --> 01:10:51,335
Inshallah.

792
01:10:53,395 --> 01:10:59,115
My sheik. my children.
An evangel!

793
01:11:02,175 --> 01:11:07,935
You'll have another sibling.
Our family is growing.

794
01:11:09,935 --> 01:11:12,985
We are growing in numbers.
Thank Allah!

795
01:11:13,355 --> 01:11:15,065
Thank Allah!

796
01:11:15,085 --> 01:11:19,125
Mashallah. Mashallah.

797
01:11:19,745 --> 01:11:21,605
Thank Allah.

798
01:11:23,385 --> 01:11:25,935
-Thank Allah.
-Thank Allah.

799
01:11:31,265 --> 01:11:35,825
May Allah keep the parents
around the baby, Osman Bey.

800
01:11:35,865 --> 01:11:38,425
Amin, my sheik.
Amin. Inshallah.

801
01:11:38,725 --> 01:11:41,285
May it come with fortune, Osman Bey.

802
01:11:41,605 --> 01:11:43,385
Amin, my Malhun.

803
01:11:44,025 --> 01:11:45,805
Congratulations, Osman Bey.

804
01:11:45,815 --> 01:11:48,375
May Allah bless it.

805
01:11:48,375 --> 01:11:49,905
Thank you.

806
01:11:50,005 --> 01:11:52,285
We'll have another sibling, huh?

807
01:11:53,295 --> 01:11:56,345
If you allow it, I want
to see my mother.

808
01:11:57,455 --> 01:12:00,155
Alahaddin. Wait, son.

809
01:12:00,345 --> 01:12:02,075
Eat first.

810
01:12:02,115 --> 01:12:04,435
You'll see your mother
after she rests.

811
01:12:09,385 --> 01:12:12,075
Come on now.
Enjoy it.

812
01:12:12,205 --> 01:12:14,705
With the name of Allah.

813
01:12:14,705 --> 01:12:17,475
Fatma was crying about beying
the youngest.

814
01:12:18,175 --> 01:12:20,955
Now you won't be the youngest.

815
01:12:21,325 --> 01:12:24,165
My prayers are answered,
my sheik grandfather.

816
01:12:24,925 --> 01:12:27,725
I'll be an older sister!

817
01:12:27,915 --> 01:12:29,415
Mashallah to you.

818
01:12:30,415 --> 01:12:33,405
You couldn't stay the smallest
forever!

819
01:12:37,215 --> 01:12:41,085
-May I enter, my bey?
-Come in!

820
01:12:46,525 --> 01:12:50,975
My bey, Kosses is here. He wants to
talk to you about something important.

821
01:12:52,495 --> 01:12:54,785
Why are you keeping him outside?
Take him in.

822
01:13:00,505 --> 01:13:03,205
Come on now.
With the name of Allah.

823
01:13:10,595 --> 01:13:11,865
My tiger.

824
01:13:19,485 --> 01:13:22,285
Oh, my Gündüz Bey.

825
01:13:25,335 --> 01:13:26,855
As he was a brave bey...

826
01:13:27,545 --> 01:13:29,695
he was also a merciful father.

827
01:13:30,505 --> 01:13:35,595
He was destined to see his son Aktimur
and the conquest of İnegöl.

828
01:13:41,235 --> 01:13:43,395
Salam Alaikum, brothers.

829
01:13:43,465 --> 01:13:46,315
-Alaikum Salam.
-Alaikum Salam.

830
01:13:49,265 --> 01:13:50,765
With the name of Allah.

831
01:13:52,135 --> 01:13:53,865
He was an older brother
to me.

832
01:13:54,435 --> 01:13:58,025
From now, Aktimur is mine
to protect.

833
01:14:02,075 --> 01:14:05,325
He will be at ease, right?

834
01:14:05,415 --> 01:14:10,195
Sure, he made it home for us
as he gave his life there.

835
01:14:11,235 --> 01:14:13,255
And he was buried there.

836
01:14:14,135 --> 01:14:16,955
Gündüz Bey. May he rest in peace.

837
01:14:17,175 --> 01:14:19,035
Amin.

838
01:14:19,545 --> 01:14:21,075
Amin.

839
01:14:23,635 --> 01:14:28,195
Lord Kosses sent you regards.

840
01:14:28,835 --> 01:14:35,395
Since his castle was taken,
Kosses isn't a lord, brother.

841
01:14:38,525 --> 01:14:43,805
He is a valiant sharpening his sword
for battle, just like us.

842
01:14:45,635 --> 01:14:48,545
You are right, Boran.
You are right.

843
01:14:49,595 --> 01:14:52,725
True. He is more valiant than
many valiants.

844
01:14:52,965 --> 01:14:55,795
He is an alp who'll go
to battles.

845
01:14:57,355 --> 01:15:01,235
Lord Kosses isn't a Muslim.
How can he be an all?

846
01:15:03,545 --> 01:15:07,555
Maybe he isn't now.
But who can know tomorrow, Şamil?

847
01:15:08,765 --> 01:15:12,015
One day you look and see
him burning with the flames of Islam.

848
01:15:13,795 --> 01:15:16,325
Maybe more Muslim than any of us?

849
01:15:18,675 --> 01:15:21,395
Thank you, Brother Boran.
Inshallah.

850
01:15:21,815 --> 01:15:23,645
Inshallah, brother.

851
01:15:33,115 --> 01:15:35,175
What will we say to Osman Bey?

852
01:15:35,515 --> 01:15:39,005
We won't hold the father responsible
for a child's disrespect.

853
01:15:39,705 --> 01:15:42,165
Ali Bey gave the answer.
It's not our business now.

854
01:15:42,975 --> 01:15:44,435
What are they after?

855
01:15:45,245 --> 01:15:47,655
They are both ill-intentioned.

856
01:15:50,515 --> 01:15:54,605
May Allah give him a long life but
when Ali Bey passes away...

857
01:15:55,885 --> 01:15:58,265
if he gets the throne,
there will be troubles.

858
01:15:58,735 --> 01:16:01,565
It's easier to feel sorrow
for one of your own, Konur.

859
01:16:03,005 --> 01:16:07,125
But feeling good about his victory
takes courage.

860
01:16:07,965 --> 01:16:12,965
It's unfortunate that those who are of
our own blood isn't feeling good.

861
01:16:17,395 --> 01:16:20,095
We know Mustafa Bey's wound.
He is offended.

862
01:16:21,555 --> 01:16:24,085
It's atabey Ahmed who is scratching
his wound.

863
01:16:24,155 --> 01:16:25,875
He gives him all the ideas.

864
01:16:25,875 --> 01:16:27,415
Whatever.

865
01:16:27,735 --> 01:16:30,025
Our duty is to be careful.

866
01:16:30,665 --> 01:16:34,245
Further speaking of this will
be gossiping. It's not us.

867
01:16:34,655 --> 01:16:37,955
Aktimur. The roads are full
of marauders.

868
01:16:38,675 --> 01:16:40,695
We'll take the caravan to Söğüt
with Konur.

869
01:16:40,965 --> 01:16:43,185
Mustafa and Ahmed will be with us.

870
01:16:43,805 --> 01:16:45,865
You'll accompany Ali Bey.

871
01:16:46,625 --> 01:16:50,155
Osman Bey always says that a great
should be greeted by a great.

872
01:16:52,185 --> 01:16:54,855
And as my martyr brother
Gündüz's son...

873
01:16:55,465 --> 01:16:57,375
you are great to me.

874
01:16:59,525 --> 01:17:02,975
I have no other wish but to be
worth to my father and uncle.

875
01:17:03,405 --> 01:17:06,405
With my life, Turgut Bey.

876
01:17:06,465 --> 01:17:07,965
Thank you.

877
01:17:21,375 --> 01:17:22,915
Insolent!

878
01:17:24,135 --> 01:17:26,685
They don't know their words
or moves!

879
01:17:28,255 --> 01:17:30,795
But I know what to do.

880
01:17:31,065 --> 01:17:34,635
Know how to control your
wrath first, Mustafa.

881
01:17:34,675 --> 01:17:36,735
This is the bey's way.

882
01:17:37,855 --> 01:17:40,635
The bey's way is attacking.

883
01:17:41,675 --> 01:17:44,765
Is it the bey's way to insult your son
against the others?

884
01:17:44,985 --> 01:17:51,225
Mustafa, you know how your father
respects Ertuğrul Ghazi.

885
01:17:51,995 --> 01:17:54,525
He grew up with his stories.

886
01:17:55,655 --> 01:17:58,355
That's why he trusts Osman Bey.

887
01:17:58,735 --> 01:18:00,965
He trusts Osman because he
trusts Ertuğrul.

888
01:18:01,575 --> 01:18:03,835
But he doesn't trust his own son.

889
01:18:04,175 --> 01:18:07,675
Why? Because he doesn't even trust
himself.

890
01:18:10,685 --> 01:18:14,735
He thinks it's greatness to stay
back in the shadows.

891
01:18:16,825 --> 01:18:20,345
Osman should do the conquests,
he should gain renown!

892
01:18:20,795 --> 01:18:24,335
If he says he is the state,
who will stand against him?

893
01:18:24,435 --> 01:18:26,465
You will, Mustafa.

894
01:18:26,515 --> 01:18:29,095
Before it comes to that.

895
01:18:29,175 --> 01:18:33,175
If Osman gathers more strength,
he won't just march to the west.

896
01:18:33,425 --> 01:18:35,615
He'll try to take us first.

897
01:18:36,195 --> 01:18:42,255
The weakness of Seljuks, absence
of any dominant power encourages him.

898
01:18:42,345 --> 01:18:45,485
You'll be the iron fist then, Mustafa.

899
01:18:45,605 --> 01:18:47,485
You raised me for today.

900
01:18:48,425 --> 01:18:52,395
I was raised with your fire,
not with my bey's slowness.

901
01:18:53,645 --> 01:18:56,725
Now I will burn them.

902
01:19:07,125 --> 01:19:09,455
We know Romanos' intentions.

903
01:19:09,945 --> 01:19:14,175
He wants to beat us and be a
hero in Constantinople.

904
01:19:14,435 --> 01:19:18,275
He is a very dangerous man, Osman Bey.
We need to be cautious.

905
01:19:19,755 --> 01:19:23,755
Who is he working with?
What kind of a game he is playing?

906
01:19:24,695 --> 01:19:26,835
We don't know who is he working with yet.

907
01:19:28,165 --> 01:19:31,855
But I know that he is more cunning
than the devil.

908
01:19:32,815 --> 01:19:34,845
If he didn't have an ear
among us...

909
01:19:35,305 --> 01:19:38,145
he wouldn't be so confident.

910
01:19:38,865 --> 01:19:41,675
There is a traitor sending
news to Rome.

911
01:19:44,045 --> 01:19:48,695
And when the road to Bursa opens,
he'll try to face us.

912
01:19:49,425 --> 01:19:54,685
To find it out first, it's better
to be close to Rome.

913
01:19:54,865 --> 01:19:57,395
So, I need you.

914
01:19:57,395 --> 01:20:00,545
Don't derange yourself in Bursa.

915
01:20:01,585 --> 01:20:05,305
You'll keep trading there
like a merchant.

916
01:20:05,505 --> 01:20:08,035
Trade builds friendships.

917
01:20:09,055 --> 01:20:10,635
Don't worry.

918
01:20:11,055 --> 01:20:14,935
Our friendship with the lord
of Bursa will improve.

919
01:20:17,395 --> 01:20:19,445
Road of Bursa you said.

920
01:20:21,745 --> 01:20:24,295
Are we thinking the same thing?

921
01:20:26,825 --> 01:20:28,955
It appears so, Kosses.

922
01:20:29,585 --> 01:20:33,135
We'll take Yenişehir first.

923
01:20:34,935 --> 01:20:37,675
I'll take Yenişehir and
make it my capital.

924
01:20:38,335 --> 01:20:43,435
Then, the conquest of Bursa and many
others will be easier.

925
01:20:44,365 --> 01:20:50,785
All the secret doors in Bursa and
Yenişehir will open to you.

926
01:20:50,885 --> 01:20:52,475
Kosses.

927
01:20:53,615 --> 01:20:56,205
The weakest side of Bursa...

928
01:20:56,775 --> 01:20:59,535
the gate that should be
entered first.

929
01:21:00,055 --> 01:21:02,175
Tell me all of this.

930
01:21:04,445 --> 01:21:06,465
Don't worry, Osman Bey.

931
01:21:06,675 --> 01:21:09,845
You'll learn every detail soon.

932
01:21:10,075 --> 01:21:12,165
Let's move, then.

933
01:21:12,905 --> 01:21:14,465
Yes.

934
01:21:16,745 --> 01:21:18,795
Yes, but...

935
01:21:19,985 --> 01:21:23,195
I have to tell you something
important first.

936
01:21:43,785 --> 01:21:46,525
Why did Cebe come
to these lands?

937
01:21:46,855 --> 01:21:48,915
To die?

938
01:21:54,185 --> 01:21:58,705
To drown Turks in their
own blood!

939
01:22:06,350 --> 01:22:11,910
But you are a disgrace to Genghis Khan!

940
01:22:18,320 --> 01:22:22,900
Erlik Khan damns you!

941
01:22:33,185 --> 01:22:37,275
What does Cebe want?

942
01:22:39,015 --> 01:22:41,805
Cebe asks you!

943
01:22:42,355 --> 01:22:44,205
He wants revenge.

944
01:22:46,185 --> 01:22:50,745
Kazan Khan turned his
back on us.

945
01:22:51,715 --> 01:22:57,295
He prefered his faith over
his people.

946
01:22:58,985 --> 01:23:00,875
Cebe...

947
01:23:01,535 --> 01:23:07,935
will kill everyone behind
Kazan Khan!

948
01:23:08,805 --> 01:23:12,275
Everyone Kazan Khan
showed mercy to...

949
01:23:13,005 --> 01:23:16,745
will meet Cebe's wrath!

950
01:23:24,125 --> 01:23:27,875
Turks, Muslims...

951
01:23:29,195 --> 01:23:30,765
all of them!

952
01:23:56,145 --> 01:24:00,975
What were Osman's brainless followers
doing there, Romanos?

953
01:24:01,715 --> 01:24:04,395
We would only bait them!

954
01:24:04,575 --> 01:24:07,595
I told you to not underestimate Osman!

955
01:24:08,685 --> 01:24:11,955
It was your duty to
seek the right time.

956
01:24:16,385 --> 01:24:18,415
Osman killed many of your men.

957
01:24:19,405 --> 01:24:22,335
I hope you have enough
warriors left.

958
01:24:28,085 --> 01:24:30,985
Only the weak fall, Romanos.

959
01:24:32,165 --> 01:24:37,645
It means that the strongest
warriors are still with me.

960
01:24:41,245 --> 01:24:42,545
Alright.

961
01:24:43,675 --> 01:24:45,795
Then let's come to our deal.

962
01:24:59,655 --> 01:25:01,835
Finding good soldiers...

963
01:25:02,895 --> 01:25:04,825
finding gold...

964
01:25:05,595 --> 01:25:07,835
isn't easy.

965
01:25:13,695 --> 01:25:20,085
Especially if you have a giant
Mongol army behind you.

966
01:25:22,735 --> 01:25:25,655
Tell me about the gold, Romanos.

967
01:25:26,205 --> 01:25:28,875
Slaying the Turks is our job.

968
01:25:29,615 --> 01:25:34,765
Until no Turk and no Muslim
is left in these lands...

969
01:25:34,785 --> 01:25:37,275
I won't sheathe my sword.

970
01:25:39,705 --> 01:25:41,855
I'll kill the damned Turks...

971
01:25:42,155 --> 01:25:43,855
and get gold.

972
01:25:44,125 --> 01:25:46,955
I think it's a good teal.

973
01:25:47,885 --> 01:25:49,995
You'll raze here.

974
01:25:51,175 --> 01:25:54,895
You'll amuse Osman and keep
him behind you.

975
01:25:56,005 --> 01:25:58,195
Until the Byzantine army
comes...

976
01:25:58,465 --> 01:26:01,595
Osman shouldn't be able to
prepare.

977
01:26:02,705 --> 01:26:04,085
So...

978
01:26:05,525 --> 01:26:07,655
do what you know the best.

979
01:26:09,455 --> 01:26:14,155
Burn. Destroy.

980
01:26:14,855 --> 01:26:16,315
Kill.

981
01:26:17,585 --> 01:26:19,975
Give hell to the Turks.

982
01:26:27,105 --> 01:26:31,525
I'm holding the head of the
last Turk who disobeyed me.

983
01:26:33,135 --> 01:26:35,695
He would tell me what to do.

984
01:26:38,585 --> 01:26:40,965
Don't talk high.

985
01:26:41,875 --> 01:26:43,465
So that you can keep talking.

986
01:27:03,325 --> 01:27:06,795
I trust you, Cebe.

987
01:27:08,875 --> 01:27:11,165
You will kill them.

988
01:27:13,425 --> 01:27:17,295
I will kill Osman.

989
01:27:20,655 --> 01:27:30,245
The name of Kayı will be forgotten.

990
01:27:31,125 --> 01:27:32,665
Tomorrow is a big day.

991
01:27:34,935 --> 01:27:36,965
I'll expect news from you.

992
01:27:46,545 --> 01:27:48,185
I take an oath...

993
01:27:49,875 --> 01:27:54,975
I'll drink their blood with the skull
of a different Turkmen everyday.

994
01:28:08,605 --> 01:28:15,155
You are finally speaking what your
heart wanted for years, Kosses.

995
01:28:16,705 --> 01:28:19,525
I wanted to be sure, Sheik Edebali.

996
01:28:21,725 --> 01:28:23,225
I've read a lot.

997
01:28:23,855 --> 01:28:25,385
I've thought a lot.

998
01:28:26,685 --> 01:28:30,115
Lately, my heart wasn't in peace.

999
01:28:31,205 --> 01:28:36,805
The only thing that will give
me peace is Islam.

1000
01:28:39,895 --> 01:28:44,255
You already declared your faith
in your hearth, it seems.

1001
01:28:48,915 --> 01:28:53,465
Now, you'll say it with your heart.

1002
01:29:02,765 --> 01:29:08,765
I bear witness that there is no god
but Allah...

1003
01:29:12,175 --> 01:29:24,675
and I bear witness that Muhammad
is the servant and Messenger of Allah.

1004
01:29:33,695 --> 01:29:35,505
May it be blessed.

1005
01:29:38,175 --> 01:29:40,195
May it be blessed.

1006
01:29:40,545 --> 01:29:42,615
May it be blessed.

1007
01:29:45,765 --> 01:29:47,475
I'm grateful.

1008
01:29:49,535 --> 01:29:51,755
I found this path thanks to you.

1009
01:29:52,145 --> 01:29:55,025
The path was in you, Kosses.

1010
01:29:55,455 --> 01:29:57,335
Allah destined you to it.

1011
01:29:59,405 --> 01:30:04,065
Your heart wanted to be on
the right path. It happened.

1012
01:30:04,935 --> 01:30:08,585
You will live as a Muslim...

1013
01:30:09,265 --> 01:30:13,725
and give your last breath as a believer,
inshallah.

1014
01:30:13,975 --> 01:30:15,495
Amin.

1015
01:30:16,245 --> 01:30:17,765
Amin.

1016
01:30:19,425 --> 01:30:22,015
With the name of Allah.

1017
01:30:25,975 --> 01:30:30,535
Kosses. You were my brother
for life.

1018
01:30:30,945 --> 01:30:33,065
Now you are my brother
in faith too.

1019
01:30:33,995 --> 01:30:35,885
Thank Allah.

1020
01:30:36,285 --> 01:30:39,185
We fought shoulder to shoulder
on the battlefield.

1021
01:30:39,505 --> 01:30:41,425
Now we take sides as an ummah.

1022
01:30:41,425 --> 01:30:43,235
Thank Allah.

1023
01:30:49,795 --> 01:30:52,065
Thank Allah.

1024
01:30:54,515 --> 01:30:57,075
I'm going to Bursa as a Muslim.

1025
01:30:57,865 --> 01:31:00,095
If I can't return...

1026
01:31:00,965 --> 01:31:02,775
give me your blessing.

1027
01:31:03,545 --> 01:31:05,075
It's yours.

1028
01:31:05,685 --> 01:31:07,195
It's yours.

1029
01:31:09,005 --> 01:31:10,595
May Allah protect you.

1030
01:31:10,635 --> 01:31:12,165
Inshallah...

1031
01:31:12,165 --> 01:31:16,885
with your helps, we'll take Yenişehir
and Bursa.

1032
01:31:18,895 --> 01:31:22,825
But you won't come.

1033
01:31:23,315 --> 01:31:25,555
You'll wait for us in Bursa.

1034
01:31:27,595 --> 01:31:29,175
Alright.

1035
01:31:30,385 --> 01:31:31,935
Alright.

1036
01:31:32,975 --> 01:31:34,275
Alright.

1037
01:31:44,545 --> 01:31:46,635
-Alps.
-My bey.

1038
01:31:47,235 --> 01:31:48,785
Here, huh?

1039
01:31:50,515 --> 01:31:53,785
My bey, she is here.
Hiding.

1040
01:32:00,665 --> 01:32:03,365
You say so...

1041
01:32:10,425 --> 01:32:15,155
Where is the most beautiful
girl of this tribe, I wonder!

1042
01:32:17,935 --> 01:32:20,195
Where is my girl Akça?

1043
01:32:20,595 --> 01:32:22,645
Where is my green-eyed one?

1044
01:32:24,405 --> 01:32:26,785
I've been searching for her
since dawn!

1045
01:32:27,495 --> 01:32:31,785
She wouldn't go anywhere without
seeing her father, but...

1046
01:32:35,855 --> 01:32:37,415
Anyway.

1047
01:32:37,585 --> 01:32:44,825
Let's see who'll be the prettiest girl
of the tribe.

1048
01:32:47,955 --> 01:32:50,355
If you have another girl...

1049
01:32:50,355 --> 01:32:54,815
she'll be the prettiest girl in
this tribe.

1050
01:33:01,345 --> 01:33:04,095
Let her be.
Let her be, my daughter.

1051
01:33:04,515 --> 01:33:06,435
You will be her older sister.

1052
01:33:09,605 --> 01:33:10,975
Come here.

1053
01:33:21,465 --> 01:33:22,845
I'm here.

1054
01:33:23,855 --> 01:33:25,335
Look at her!

1055
01:33:30,115 --> 01:33:31,785
Fatma.

1056
01:33:34,825 --> 01:33:36,095
Come.

1057
01:33:39,605 --> 01:33:41,205
I'm here.

1058
01:33:46,955 --> 01:33:48,835
My little sheep!

1059
01:33:49,355 --> 01:33:51,395
You'll have a sibling.

1060
01:33:51,565 --> 01:33:55,455
As your older brothers and sisters
took care of you.

1061
01:33:55,665 --> 01:33:57,555
So will you.

1062
01:33:58,745 --> 01:34:00,255
You are an older sister now.

1063
01:34:01,075 --> 01:34:03,025
Alright. I'll take care
of her but...

1064
01:34:03,345 --> 01:34:06,335
I grew up...

1065
01:34:06,595 --> 01:34:08,295
I'll have a sibling too...

1066
01:34:08,965 --> 01:34:13,575
then, like my older brothers
and sisters, I want weapons too!

1067
01:34:13,715 --> 01:34:15,375
Look at her!

1068
01:34:19,385 --> 01:34:22,315
My girl, just ask for a weapon.

1069
01:34:22,335 --> 01:34:24,985
I'll have the most beautiful one
forged for you!

1070
01:34:26,555 --> 01:34:27,795
Deal?

1071
01:34:28,705 --> 01:34:30,235
I want a horse too.

1072
01:34:34,165 --> 01:34:36,015
Fatma.

1073
01:34:36,985 --> 01:34:39,315
But you'll have a weapon
forged. You promised!

1074
01:34:39,505 --> 01:34:43,085
Yes. I'll have the prettiest
one forged for you.

1075
01:34:43,185 --> 01:34:44,735
Come on.

1076
01:34:44,855 --> 01:34:48,375
After I learn how to use it,
I'll join the sisters.

1077
01:34:49,035 --> 01:34:50,735
Look at you!

1078
01:34:51,455 --> 01:34:53,265
Mashallah to her.

1079
01:34:53,265 --> 01:34:55,155
Mashallah.
Come.

1080
01:34:55,415 --> 01:34:56,775
Come.

1081
01:34:56,815 --> 01:34:59,295
Let's say I gave the weapon.
What will happen?

1082
01:34:59,515 --> 01:35:01,065
I'll go to war.

1083
01:35:01,115 --> 01:35:02,885
Look at you!

1084
01:35:03,105 --> 01:35:05,875
-Do you hear it, alps? To war!
-Mashallah.

1085
01:35:05,875 --> 01:35:07,895
Mashallah, my bey.

1086
01:35:58,055 --> 01:35:59,605
My bey.

1087
01:36:00,145 --> 01:36:02,175
I found it while I was tracing.

1088
01:36:02,525 --> 01:36:04,855
Mongol commander Cebe.

1089
01:36:06,815 --> 01:36:09,455
He wants an audience.

1090
01:37:04,655 --> 01:37:09,715
Finally we met, Osman.
Bey.

1091
01:37:14,105 --> 01:37:16,115
I heard a lot about you in Konya.

1092
01:37:18,595 --> 01:37:21,345
I'm here with Sultan Alahaddin's order.

1093
01:37:28,115 --> 01:37:34,375
I rode here, chasing the fleeing
Mongol soldiers of Sülemiş Revolt.

1094
01:37:34,995 --> 01:37:37,265
My warriors set camp at the valley.

1095
01:37:39,175 --> 01:37:41,435
I'm here until I find those
marauders.

1096
01:37:52,695 --> 01:37:55,025
What do you want from me?

1097
01:38:05,785 --> 01:38:08,495
No one knows here better than you,
Osman Bey.

1098
01:38:10,185 --> 01:38:13,205
I want you to help me find them.

1099
01:38:16,565 --> 01:38:21,345
As you read it. That's how Sultan
Alahaddin orders.

1100
01:38:24,435 --> 01:38:25,815
I'll help.

1101
01:38:26,755 --> 01:38:28,635
I'll help, surely.

1102
01:38:30,095 --> 01:38:37,605
But Sultan Alahaddin, why is he sending
a Mongol commander for this?

1103
01:38:40,015 --> 01:38:42,465
Are there no soldiers left
in Konya?

1104
01:38:53,835 --> 01:38:56,555
You wouldn't know why, Osman Bey.

1105
01:38:58,345 --> 01:39:02,785
And I don't know why the Turkmens
I saw on the road are coming to you.

1106
01:39:07,875 --> 01:39:13,145
Sülemiş revolted for his own benefit.

1107
01:39:14,565 --> 01:39:17,135
If Kazan Khan had made him the governor...

1108
01:39:17,895 --> 01:39:19,985
there would be no revolt.

1109
01:39:20,265 --> 01:39:23,005
Then he fled to the Mamelukes like
a coward!

1110
01:39:27,535 --> 01:39:29,145
Wouldn't you be afraid?

1111
01:39:29,435 --> 01:39:30,755
Never!

1112
01:39:32,015 --> 01:39:33,545
Cebe...

1113
01:39:34,015 --> 01:39:37,325
never leaves before finishing
what he started.

1114
01:39:39,075 --> 01:39:41,575
I will find those marauders...

1115
01:39:41,885 --> 01:39:44,145
and make them pay.

1116
01:39:54,025 --> 01:39:57,565
My bey, Ali Bey is coming.

1117
01:40:04,785 --> 01:40:06,525
My alps will accompany you.

1118
01:40:07,465 --> 01:40:09,005
Then...

1119
01:40:09,345 --> 01:40:11,105
let's find those marauders.

1120
01:40:27,025 --> 01:40:28,865
-Cerkutay.
-My bey.

1121
01:40:32,585 --> 01:40:34,805
Stay close to him.

1122
01:40:36,305 --> 01:40:37,885
As my bey orders.

1123
01:41:38,845 --> 01:41:40,365
Alps!

1124
01:41:40,425 --> 01:41:41,985
Be cautious.

1125
01:42:01,225 --> 01:42:03,765
We trust you to get on
the way.

1126
01:42:03,845 --> 01:42:06,165
Taking İnegöl isn't enough, it seems.

1127
01:42:07,085 --> 01:42:11,165
If you can't control some bandits,
how can you control İnegöl?

1128
01:42:12,645 --> 01:42:14,585
You are speaking over your position.

1129
01:42:15,365 --> 01:42:17,545
But I'll not hear it because
of your pain.

1130
01:42:19,285 --> 01:42:20,805
Now stop the haste.

1131
01:42:20,805 --> 01:42:22,805
Whoever done this...

1132
01:42:22,805 --> 01:42:24,805
will pay for it!

1133
01:42:25,145 --> 01:42:28,335
While you were greeting us with
smooth talk in the caravansarai...

1134
01:42:28,335 --> 01:42:30,765
our alps were dying here.

1135
01:42:30,765 --> 01:42:32,785
Is this how you protect
the roads?

1136
01:42:33,525 --> 01:42:35,245
Shame on you!

1137
01:42:35,805 --> 01:42:38,805
Now, think about what you'll
say to Ali Bey.

1138
01:42:44,885 --> 01:42:46,425
Don't worry.

1139
01:42:46,585 --> 01:42:48,965
We'll find and punish
the responsible.

1140
01:42:49,045 --> 01:42:51,165
But now, it's time to chase
those traitors.

1141
01:42:52,305 --> 01:42:55,425
Wasting time with words
won't do us good.

1142
01:42:56,565 --> 01:42:59,325
Kutan, go to the tribe and
inform Osman Bey.

1143
01:43:00,045 --> 01:43:02,745
We'll trace the traitors
who did this.

1144
01:43:02,905 --> 01:43:04,745
Then catch up with us.

1145
01:43:04,765 --> 01:43:06,325
As you order, my bey.

1146
01:43:10,405 --> 01:43:11,885
Recover soon, sisters.

1147
01:43:14,685 --> 01:43:16,185
Thank you, my bey.

1148
01:43:34,345 --> 01:43:37,085
Welcome, Ali Bey!

1149
01:43:40,885 --> 01:43:43,425
Welcome!
Welcome!

1150
01:43:43,525 --> 01:43:45,525
Welcome!

1151
01:43:46,885 --> 01:43:50,245
Welcome! Welcome, my bey!

1152
01:43:54,445 --> 01:43:57,125
Welcome!

1153
01:43:57,125 --> 01:44:01,385
Welcome!
Welcome!

1154
01:44:02,165 --> 01:44:05,025
Welcome!

1155
01:44:08,125 --> 01:44:11,285
Welcome! Welcome!

1156
01:44:19,265 --> 01:44:22,005
Welcome! You honored us!

1157
01:44:25,265 --> 01:44:31,385
Welcome! Welcome!

1158
01:45:36,805 --> 01:45:38,625
Mashallah!

1159
01:45:46,565 --> 01:45:48,085
Come on, now.

1160
01:45:58,685 --> 01:46:00,245
Salam Alaikum.

1161
01:46:00,805 --> 01:46:02,345
Alaikum Salam!

1162
01:46:08,405 --> 01:46:10,145
Welcome, Ali Bey.

1163
01:46:10,245 --> 01:46:11,785
Thank you, Osman Bey.

1164
01:46:11,840 --> 01:46:14,380
What a greeting that was!

1165
01:46:14,740 --> 01:46:16,760
Mashallah to your alps.

1166
01:46:18,740 --> 01:46:22,800
And they are right up there
with the alps.

1167
01:46:23,240 --> 01:46:24,800
True.

1168
01:46:25,160 --> 01:46:29,280
It's certain that they'll be valiants
just like their father Osman.

1169
01:46:31,420 --> 01:46:33,180
Inshallah.

1170
01:46:33,180 --> 01:46:35,720
Inshallah. Come on.
Come on.

1171
01:46:45,400 --> 01:46:47,100
Little sister!

1172
01:46:48,220 --> 01:46:51,080
You will also be capable.
I can tell!

1173
01:46:52,820 --> 01:46:54,900
Your great grandmother, Mother Haime.

1174
01:46:55,300 --> 01:46:56,800
She was very capable.

1175
01:46:59,120 --> 01:47:02,520
You seem a little shy, huh?

1176
01:47:03,760 --> 01:47:05,520
She is shy at first times.

1177
01:47:05,520 --> 01:47:08,020
But she is very vocal, Ali Bey.

1178
01:47:08,020 --> 01:47:11,040
When he gets comfortalbe,
she gets everyone tired.

1179
01:47:12,480 --> 01:47:15,680
May Allah protect your children.

1180
01:47:15,680 --> 01:47:17,680
-Amin.
-Amin.

1181
01:47:19,240 --> 01:47:20,760
May Allah bless you.

1182
01:47:20,800 --> 01:47:22,100
Thank you.

1183
01:47:22,100 --> 01:47:24,600
You honored our tribe, Ali Bey.

1184
01:47:24,600 --> 01:47:27,140
I'm honored. Thank you.

1185
01:47:27,340 --> 01:47:29,640
You took a long way.

1186
01:47:29,700 --> 01:47:31,440
You must be tired.

1187
01:47:31,440 --> 01:47:34,160
Eat our meal,
drink our ayran.

1188
01:47:34,580 --> 01:47:35,880
Let's get in.

1189
01:47:35,880 --> 01:47:37,880
-Come.
-Thank you.

1190
01:47:41,285 --> 01:47:43,825
It's been a long time since I last
ate Kayı meal.

1191
01:47:44,265 --> 01:47:45,785
I missed it!

1192
01:47:45,785 --> 01:47:47,345
Thank you!

1193
01:48:29,525 --> 01:48:32,105
They separated to get rid
of us.

1194
01:48:32,905 --> 01:48:35,485
Konur, go this way with
the alps.

1195
01:48:35,865 --> 01:48:37,625
We'll go this way with you.

1196
01:48:37,625 --> 01:48:39,625
Be cautious.
Come on.

1197
01:48:48,385 --> 01:48:50,645
Thank Allah for this reunion, Ali Bey.

1198
01:48:50,665 --> 01:48:53,205
Thank Allah, Osman Bey.
Thank Allah.

1199
01:48:53,825 --> 01:48:59,025
While the Mongols are around,
my caravan was in danger but...

1200
01:48:59,805 --> 01:49:02,905
Turgut Bey and Konur Alps's
escort...

1201
01:49:02,905 --> 01:49:04,905
gave us security.

1202
01:49:05,885 --> 01:49:07,185
Thank you.

1203
01:49:07,185 --> 01:49:09,185
Thank you.
Thank you.

1204
01:49:09,365 --> 01:49:11,425
You are our friend.

1205
01:49:11,425 --> 01:49:15,205
Of course, you would do the same for us.

1206
01:49:18,705 --> 01:49:21,665
The Mongols fleeing Sülemiş Revolt.

1207
01:49:22,105 --> 01:49:23,985
They came here.

1208
01:49:24,265 --> 01:49:28,565
They are raiding all the caravans.

1209
01:49:30,405 --> 01:49:33,645
And Rome is sharpening its
fangs against us.

1210
01:49:33,845 --> 01:49:40,125
The conquest of İnegöl must've
made Constantinople feel sick.

1211
01:49:43,165 --> 01:49:45,785
As you ruin the enemy like this...

1212
01:49:45,785 --> 01:49:47,785
we feel prouder.

1213
01:49:47,865 --> 01:49:49,405
Thank you.

1214
01:49:49,405 --> 01:49:52,385
But we aren't doing the conquests
for ourselves.

1215
01:49:52,785 --> 01:49:54,845
Firstly, for Allah's approval...

1216
01:49:54,845 --> 01:50:00,305
and then, for the prosperity of the
Muslims and all the oppressed.

1217
01:50:01,365 --> 01:50:04,685
You carry your ancestors' hearts.

1218
01:50:05,325 --> 01:50:06,685
Otherwise...

1219
01:50:06,685 --> 01:50:10,005
...the conquest of Inegol
would be impossible.

1220
01:50:10,525 --> 01:50:12,105
Thank you.

1221
01:50:12,545 --> 01:50:14,065
Thank you.

1222
01:50:18,965 --> 01:50:21,005
But Inegol's conquest...

1223
01:50:21,725 --> 01:50:23,805
...is not enough for our dreams.

1224
01:50:25,205 --> 01:50:28,225
What is that you thinking of, Osman Bey?

1225
01:50:34,145 --> 01:50:35,725
Bursa.

1226
01:50:47,665 --> 01:50:49,485
Bursa is our target.

1227
01:51:01,825 --> 01:51:03,365
Sons.

1228
01:51:26,450 --> 01:51:28,450
Tracks end here

1229
01:51:29,290 --> 01:51:30,990
But why?

1230
01:51:36,950 --> 01:51:39,190
You neither protect our goods...

1231
01:51:39,650 --> 01:51:41,870
...nor you are able to track.

1232
01:51:42,990 --> 01:51:47,590
You are supposed to be the boss of Inegol
but doesn't seem like that, Turgut Bey.

1233
01:51:49,730 --> 01:51:51,450
What is your intention?

1234
01:51:52,630 --> 01:51:55,210
Do you want to drive me crazy and
get yourself killed?

1235
01:51:55,210 --> 01:51:58,710
My intention is to tell the truths
instead of keeping them in my mind.

1236
01:51:59,350 --> 01:52:02,090
You are not as powerful as you seem.

1237
01:52:03,030 --> 01:52:06,230
You are not even strong enough to
protect your things.

1238
01:52:06,230 --> 01:52:08,750
You are just following a dumb man.

1239
01:52:08,750 --> 01:52:12,250
That man you call dumb is my brother
Osman Bey, whose way is my way.

1240
01:52:12,250 --> 01:52:14,250
Weigh your words, old man.

1241
01:52:14,250 --> 01:52:16,250
Turgut Bey.

1242
01:52:16,510 --> 01:52:18,550
You talk too much.

1243
01:52:18,770 --> 01:52:20,770
Face me if you can!

1244
01:52:26,290 --> 01:52:28,170
You are too young.
Stop it.

1245
01:52:28,210 --> 01:52:30,250
Do not get yourself killed here.

1246
01:52:45,590 --> 01:52:47,670
It's poisonous.

1247
01:52:49,190 --> 01:52:51,190
It can even kill a lion.

1248
01:53:09,410 --> 01:53:11,490
Turgut won't die.

1249
01:53:11,490 --> 01:53:13,490
He will suffer.

1250
01:53:15,110 --> 01:53:18,010
Cebe's plan will work precisely.

1251
01:53:25,250 --> 01:53:27,790
Meet my poison, Turgut.

1252
01:53:29,970 --> 01:53:32,010
These are not from us, Alps!

1253
01:53:32,010 --> 01:53:34,010
Draw your swords!

1254
01:53:42,970 --> 01:53:46,970
You are not strong at all, Turgut Bey.

1255
01:54:14,030 --> 01:54:16,710
Stop, what are you doing?!
Their mouths are tight!

1256
01:54:31,650 --> 01:54:33,170
Mustafa should be safe.

1257
01:54:33,370 --> 01:54:35,380
Or our plan will be wasted.

1258
01:54:35,380 --> 01:54:37,210
Osman would see the truth.

1259
01:54:37,210 --> 01:54:39,210
Ali would see the truth!

1260
01:54:50,830 --> 01:54:52,840
I will tell you only one thing.

1261
01:54:57,710 --> 01:55:02,270
The thightest mouth
is a dead man's mouth.

1262
01:55:04,430 --> 01:55:06,950
You don't need to live.

1263
01:55:08,030 --> 01:55:12,610
We are here for avenge.
You are here for gold.

1264
01:55:14,800 --> 01:55:16,850
Osman wouldn't believe it...

1265
01:55:17,000 --> 01:55:19,540
...if Ahmet was alive.

1266
01:55:19,650 --> 01:55:21,210
Well said, Aizek.

1267
01:55:21,280 --> 01:55:22,780
You are smart.

1268
01:55:22,780 --> 01:55:24,780
You are smarter than Arius.

1269
01:55:27,680 --> 01:55:30,970
Thousands of swords are not necessary
in order to win a battle.

1270
01:55:33,480 --> 01:55:38,250
Sometimes just a dagger is enough.

1271
01:55:41,400 --> 01:55:43,100
Sir, someone is approaching.

1272
01:55:45,630 --> 01:55:47,210
Okay.

1273
01:55:47,600 --> 01:55:51,980
Let's leave then.
Let them kill each other.

1274
01:56:03,185 --> 01:56:04,925
You trace well.

1275
01:56:05,785 --> 01:56:08,585
Do they teach how to trace in Kayi?

1276
01:56:09,385 --> 01:56:16,075
I learned how to send cruels to hell
in Kayi tribe.

1277
01:56:18,815 --> 01:56:21,375
I learned how to trace way before.

1278
01:56:22,355 --> 01:56:24,945
When did you learn it?
Has it been a very long time?

1279
01:56:25,045 --> 01:56:27,045
Why are you keep asking?

1280
01:56:32,475 --> 01:56:35,025
Are you jealous of my skills?

1281
01:56:40,555 --> 01:56:42,615
Mongols, huh.

1282
01:56:45,245 --> 01:56:51,695
No one can trace like a Mongol.
Neither on land nor at sky.

1283
01:56:53,925 --> 01:56:56,445
This way.

1284
01:57:03,295 --> 01:57:05,885
Yenisehir is key for Bursa.

1285
01:57:07,075 --> 01:57:11,585
This is why I will conquer Yenisehir first.

1286
01:57:14,215 --> 01:57:18,925
But Ali Bey, I need your support.

1287
01:57:20,675 --> 01:57:27,215
I would be wasting my Bey post if I
didn't participate in such a blessed duty.

1288
01:57:29,875 --> 01:57:32,215
I stand with you.

1289
01:57:34,755 --> 01:57:36,315
Eyvallah (thank you)

1290
01:57:36,755 --> 01:57:44,255
You gathered the bravest Alps
from Caucasus to these lands.

1291
01:57:45,475 --> 01:57:48,815
They praised those valiants very much.

1292
01:57:48,815 --> 01:57:51,355
I would like to see them.

1293
01:57:51,355 --> 01:57:53,355
Can I come in, my Bey?

1294
01:57:54,875 --> 01:57:56,695
Here they are.

1295
01:57:58,155 --> 01:57:59,725
Come!

1296
01:58:10,815 --> 01:58:12,855
Eagles are famous in Caucasus.

1297
01:58:13,695 --> 01:58:15,245
Turhan.

1298
01:58:15,415 --> 01:58:20,445
He killed those who wanted to kill me.

1299
01:58:23,585 --> 01:58:27,785
Samil.
He has been with us for a quite long time.

1300
01:58:27,785 --> 01:58:32,985
He hunt them all like an eagle
in Inegol.

1301
01:58:34,075 --> 01:58:36,795
Hay Masha Allah valiants.

1302
01:58:37,955 --> 01:58:40,275
Tell me how it winds...

1303
01:58:40,275 --> 01:58:42,555
...in Caucasus.

1304
01:58:43,095 --> 01:58:46,415
When a drop of blood spills here...

1305
01:58:46,895 --> 01:58:49,845
The same drop of
blood spills in Caucasus as well.

1306
01:58:50,525 --> 01:58:53,295
Both our pain and happiness are shared.

1307
01:58:56,215 --> 01:58:57,745
Masha Allah
(praise be)

1308
01:58:59,325 --> 01:59:00,825
My valiant.

1309
01:59:01,095 --> 01:59:03,625
You came from Susha.

1310
01:59:03,925 --> 01:59:07,295
What brought you here?

1311
01:59:09,525 --> 01:59:12,055
What brings a Turk is a call for war.

1312
01:59:12,055 --> 01:59:15,315
I am here to become a Ghazi,
a martyr if destined.

1313
01:59:19,695 --> 01:59:21,755
There are many Beys.

1314
01:59:21,755 --> 01:59:24,125
Is it only Osman Bey who is fighting?

1315
01:59:25,925 --> 01:59:28,925
Why do you stand with Osman Bey?

1316
01:59:31,385 --> 01:59:32,675
There are many Beys.

1317
01:59:32,675 --> 01:59:34,185
They are all fighting.

1318
01:59:34,185 --> 01:59:36,875
Why are you in Osman Bey's tent?

1319
01:59:40,295 --> 01:59:44,095
I came to congratulate his conquests.

1320
01:59:44,095 --> 01:59:48,555
We are here to spill our blood,
die in those conquests!

1321
01:59:49,095 --> 01:59:50,925
You talk about other Beys.

1322
01:59:50,925 --> 01:59:52,925
All are turning their back on each other.

1323
01:59:52,925 --> 01:59:56,015
But Osman Bey
always goes forward.

1324
01:59:58,525 --> 02:00:00,525
Both east and west are ours.

1325
02:00:00,525 --> 02:00:04,185
We will fight until the flag of Islam
raises in the whole world.

1326
02:00:05,725 --> 02:00:08,015
May your way be open.

1327
02:00:09,015 --> 02:00:10,385
Eyvallah.
(Thank you)

1328
02:00:11,785 --> 02:00:13,615
Masha Allah valiants.
(Praise be!)

1329
02:00:16,615 --> 02:00:18,445
Can I come in my Bey?

1330
02:00:18,445 --> 02:00:20,445
Come, Kutan.

1331
02:00:27,125 --> 02:00:28,475
My Bey.

1332
02:00:28,955 --> 02:00:31,185
They raided Ali Bey's caravan.

1333
02:00:32,325 --> 02:00:34,325
There are many deads and woundeds.

1334
02:00:35,495 --> 02:00:38,275
Shahzade Mustafa and Atabey
are after them.

1335
02:00:42,295 --> 02:00:43,675
Who?

1336
02:00:43,895 --> 02:00:46,395
Who did this, Osman Bey?

1337
02:00:53,755 --> 02:00:55,845
Looks like Mongols.

1338
02:01:00,295 --> 02:01:02,025
Calm down.

1339
02:01:02,125 --> 02:01:03,875
We'll do what we need to do.

1340
02:01:03,875 --> 02:01:06,385
How can I calm down, Osman Bey?

1341
02:01:07,495 --> 02:01:11,215
Everybody knows how much I rely on Kayis!

1342
02:01:11,815 --> 02:01:13,215
Am I wrong?

1343
02:01:15,355 --> 02:01:17,215
Oh, Osman Bey.

1344
02:01:17,475 --> 02:01:23,045
Do not set your eyes on forward
before you provide the security.

1345
02:01:27,415 --> 02:01:29,445
We have enemies everywhere.

1346
02:01:30,475 --> 02:01:32,645
You were careless.

1347
02:01:34,275 --> 02:01:36,615
My Creator gave us power...

1348
02:01:38,355 --> 02:01:41,475
...we ended the cruelty in this land.

1349
02:01:43,125 --> 02:01:48,685
Whoever hurts my guests, the goods
of my guests...

1350
02:01:48,985 --> 02:01:51,015
...will pay dearly.

1351
02:01:52,755 --> 02:01:55,275
Do not worry about this.

1352
02:01:55,525 --> 02:01:57,875
I wouldn't.

1353
02:01:58,955 --> 02:02:03,495
I couldn't have felt more safe even if
I provided the security for my caravan.

1354
02:02:03,845 --> 02:02:06,585
But, the outcome.

1355
02:02:07,725 --> 02:02:10,355
I only care the outcome, Osman Bey.

1356
02:02:13,245 --> 02:02:16,295
Then be patient to see the end of things,
Ali Bey.

1357
02:02:18,495 --> 02:02:20,295
Be patient.

1358
02:03:26,925 --> 02:03:28,685
Murderer!

1359
02:03:41,245 --> 02:03:43,075
What is happening here, Turgut Bey?

1360
02:03:43,075 --> 02:03:44,605
He killed my Atabey!

1361
02:03:44,605 --> 02:03:46,315
They raided us Cerkutay.

1362
02:03:49,835 --> 02:03:52,405
There is something wrong with this arr!

1363
02:03:56,435 --> 02:03:59,485
I will kill you...

1364
02:04:01,635 --> 02:04:03,445
...to let everyone know!

1365
02:04:03,545 --> 02:04:06,855
I will blow your head!

1366
02:04:08,275 --> 02:04:09,805
Stop, Shehzade.

1367
02:04:09,885 --> 02:04:12,405
This is not the place to secure the justice!

1368
02:04:17,145 --> 02:04:19,155
If you love your life...

1369
02:04:19,175 --> 02:04:21,175
...give Turgut to me.

1370
02:04:28,455 --> 02:04:31,035
Turgut Bey will go to the tents.

1371
02:04:32,145 --> 02:04:34,155
Osman Bey will judge!

1372
02:04:35,255 --> 02:04:38,405
Whoever disobeys this rule
disobeys Osman Bey.

1373
02:04:39,715 --> 02:04:41,735
Let it be.

1374
02:04:41,775 --> 02:04:44,345
But what Turgut deserves is death!

1375
02:04:45,205 --> 02:04:49,605
If Turgut gets forgiven,
I will not step back.

1376
02:04:51,435 --> 02:04:53,005
Alps!

1377
02:04:53,045 --> 02:04:54,885
Care Turgut Bey's wound!

1378
02:04:54,885 --> 02:04:57,205
Come on, come on!

1379
02:04:57,205 --> 02:04:59,055
Come no brothers!

1380
02:05:00,655 --> 02:05:02,005
Come on!

1381
02:05:02,405 --> 02:05:03,735
Come on!

1382
02:05:11,585 --> 02:05:14,135
You have too much to worry.

1383
02:05:14,785 --> 02:05:17,785
I will keep tracing myself.

1384
02:06:47,155 --> 02:06:49,895
I will cut those who did this into slices!

1385
02:06:56,835 --> 02:07:00,555
I came to say that
Beys want to see Ali Bey...

1386
02:07:01,215 --> 02:07:04,325
...as I can see, there must be
something more important.

1387
02:07:05,015 --> 02:07:08,185
We entrusted our goods and lives.

1388
02:07:11,355 --> 02:07:14,325
Our trust is destroyed, Barkin Bey.

1389
02:07:16,295 --> 02:07:18,785
This is the important issue!

1390
02:07:19,915 --> 02:07:21,575
Stop there.

1391
02:07:47,595 --> 02:07:49,995
Devils are on their work.

1392
02:07:51,095 --> 02:07:53,555
New borders, new enemies.

1393
02:07:54,595 --> 02:07:57,175
We surely know that
we'll overcome all.

1394
02:07:59,435 --> 02:08:00,955
Inshallah.
(If Allah permits)

1395
02:08:36,695 --> 02:08:38,055
My Son!

1396
02:08:38,075 --> 02:08:40,575
Mustafa!
Son!

1397
02:08:49,455 --> 02:08:51,035
Ahmet.

1398
02:08:58,185 --> 02:09:02,245
Cerkutay! Konur!
What happened?

1399
02:09:06,825 --> 02:09:08,645
When we arrived...

1400
02:09:08,745 --> 02:09:11,265
I'll tell you what happened Osman Bey!

1401
02:09:14,225 --> 02:09:17,005
Turgut Bey who you sent
with us to protect us...

1402
02:09:17,345 --> 02:09:19,125
...killed Atabey!

1403
02:09:23,905 --> 02:09:26,445
They would say
"Kayi tribe is traitors' place"...

1404
02:09:27,145 --> 02:09:29,025
...but we didn't expect so quickly!

1405
02:09:48,905 --> 02:09:50,405
Turgut Bey?

1406
02:09:52,305 --> 02:09:53,885
Turgut Bey?

1407
02:09:57,345 --> 02:09:59,185
What the hell?

1408
02:09:59,485 --> 02:10:01,985
Cerkutay!
Konur!

1409
02:10:03,485 --> 02:10:05,005
Tell me!

1410
02:10:09,745 --> 02:10:11,245
Turgut Bey!

1411
02:10:16,825 --> 02:10:18,565
How did this happen?

1412
02:10:18,605 --> 02:10:20,185
Tell me, son!

1413
02:10:20,265 --> 02:10:23,425
We were tracing Mongols who raided us.

1414
02:10:24,105 --> 02:10:27,245
That traitor Turgut teased Atabey!

1415
02:10:27,825 --> 02:10:30,405
He stabbed him in the chest!

1416
02:10:31,085 --> 02:10:34,645
His Alps shoot arrows to me.

1417
02:10:34,845 --> 02:10:36,425
No.

1418
02:10:37,365 --> 02:10:39,165
Stop there.

1419
02:10:45,145 --> 02:10:47,145
Are these true?

1420
02:10:52,525 --> 02:10:54,105
Cerkutay!

1421
02:10:54,905 --> 02:10:56,405
Konur!

1422
02:10:56,665 --> 02:10:58,185
Tell me!

1423
02:11:01,565 --> 02:11:03,105
My Bey.

1424
02:11:06,125 --> 02:11:09,185
When we arrived...

1425
02:11:10,625 --> 02:11:12,165
Turgut Bey...

1426
02:11:13,185 --> 02:11:19,025
...was taking this dagger out
of Atabey's chest.

1427
02:11:23,305 --> 02:11:26,365
This is what we have seen, my Bey.

1428
02:11:32,045 --> 02:11:34,065
He is right, my Bey.

1429
02:11:55,205 --> 02:11:57,265
Let Turgut Bey come to himself.

1430
02:11:58,905 --> 02:12:00,925
Then we'll judge.

1431
02:12:03,385 --> 02:12:06,545
The guilt is obvious.
The guilty is obvious.

1432
02:12:07,125 --> 02:12:10,205
What is there to judge, Osman Bey?

1433
02:12:10,825 --> 02:12:13,325
You know the tradition, Ali Bey!

1434
02:12:14,685 --> 02:12:16,705
You know it better than me!

1435
02:12:16,785 --> 02:12:20,825
What I know is that reprisal is a must!

1436
02:12:23,285 --> 02:12:27,705
Life for life!
Blood for blood!

1437
02:12:28,545 --> 02:12:30,545
Ali Bey!
Ali Bey

1438
02:12:32,165 --> 02:12:34,885
Let go of me, Osman Bey!

1439
02:12:36,445 --> 02:12:38,025
Ali Bey!

1440
02:12:39,965 --> 02:12:41,485
Stop!

1441
02:12:42,545 --> 02:12:44,545
This is not a place to judge!

1442
02:12:44,805 --> 02:12:46,865
You are not to judge either!

1443
02:12:48,125 --> 02:12:49,905
This is Kayi tribe.

1444
02:12:50,525 --> 02:12:52,805
Everything goes by the justice here.

1445
02:13:19,140 --> 02:13:22,640
That's it!

1446
02:13:23,940 --> 02:13:26,440
Well done!

1447
02:13:29,000 --> 02:13:33,120
We both got the best of this case.

1448
02:13:39,300 --> 02:13:41,040
I got the best of the best.

1449
02:13:41,840 --> 02:13:45,680
I earned gold for doing what I love
to do the most, killing Turks!

1450
02:13:46,940 --> 02:13:48,720
What more can I desire?

1451
02:13:51,540 --> 02:13:53,260
But remember.

1452
02:13:54,460 --> 02:13:56,960
There are so much gold to earn.

1453
02:14:05,520 --> 02:14:07,040
Don't worry.

1454
02:14:11,020 --> 02:14:13,560
Do not let your anger blind you, Ali Bey.

1455
02:14:13,860 --> 02:14:16,400
Even the best eyes can missee here.

1456
02:14:16,940 --> 02:14:20,480
We supported you, came here.

1457
02:14:20,780 --> 02:14:23,340
First, it was about our goods.

1458
02:14:23,540 --> 02:14:25,620
We didn't care much.

1459
02:14:26,660 --> 02:14:29,160
I thought "not more important
than my son's life!"

1460
02:14:30,080 --> 02:14:31,640
But now...

1461
02:14:32,180 --> 02:14:34,720
My Mustafa is wounded.

1462
02:14:34,780 --> 02:14:39,560
Atabey Ahmet , who I considered
as a brother, is dead!

1463
02:14:40,800 --> 02:14:44,340
You protect Turgut Bey's life!

1464
02:14:44,500 --> 02:14:48,380
Do you think your men
have more value than mine!

1465
02:14:51,220 --> 02:14:52,920
Ali Bey!

1466
02:14:57,860 --> 02:15:00,360
It is not the case of whose man's life!

1467
02:15:00,900 --> 02:15:02,940
Allah is the one who gives life!

1468
02:15:12,280 --> 02:15:14,780
If this is done by Turgut Bey...

1469
02:15:16,280 --> 02:15:18,820
I will judge him.

1470
02:15:20,540 --> 02:15:23,820
The right justice is the fast justice.

1471
02:15:24,660 --> 02:15:26,700
Not the delayed justice!

1472
02:15:27,600 --> 02:15:32,100
All the men say they witnessed!

1473
02:15:32,620 --> 02:15:37,160
You don't even believe your own
Alps' words.

1474
02:15:44,740 --> 02:15:47,240
The one who judges by words...

1475
02:15:48,360 --> 02:15:50,400
...gets captivated the other day.

1476
02:15:50,480 --> 02:15:52,280
This is Kayi tribe.

1477
02:15:52,400 --> 02:15:54,200
This is the home of deceptive cases!

1478
02:15:55,680 --> 02:15:59,920
Even the truths may seem like lies!

1479
02:16:03,020 --> 02:16:05,020
Now be aware.

1480
02:16:08,400 --> 02:16:10,440
If you are not...

1481
02:16:11,400 --> 02:16:15,100
...then no one can wake you up
from the sleep of unawareness.

1482
02:16:16,200 --> 02:16:17,960
Ali Bey.

1483
02:16:23,540 --> 02:16:28,100
I will take Turgut from you, Osman Bey.

1484
02:16:28,420 --> 02:16:33,000
Either bring Turgut's head and throw
it at my feet...

1485
02:16:35,718 --> 02:16:41,240
...or we'll have a fight in which
the blood of brothers spills.

1486
02:16:47,799 --> 02:16:50,109
You always mentioned the
importance of life!

1487
02:16:51,299 --> 02:16:54,420
A thousand lives for a life!

1488
02:16:55,160 --> 02:16:56,700
Osman Bey!

1489
02:17:01,379 --> 02:17:04,920
The decision is yours now.

1490
02:17:07,860 --> 02:17:09,420
Ali Bey.

1491
02:17:10,459 --> 02:17:14,500
It is now my mission to...

1492
02:17:15,760 --> 02:17:19,299
...cut the head of whoever tries
to set you and I against each other...

1493
02:17:19,920 --> 02:17:22,240
...and throw his head at your feet.

1494
02:17:28,600 --> 02:17:30,100
Alps.

1495
02:17:52,260 --> 02:17:53,760
My Bey.

1496
02:17:57,080 --> 02:17:58,820
Turgut Bey!

1497
02:18:01,540 --> 02:18:03,280
Are you fine?

1498
02:18:03,340 --> 02:18:04,840
Osman Bey.

1499
02:18:06,580 --> 02:18:09,080
Tell me, tell me.

1500
02:18:13,600 --> 02:18:15,660
Tell me, Turgut Bey!

1501
02:18:21,200 --> 02:18:22,760
No.

1502
02:18:25,120 --> 02:18:26,620
He is not well.

1503
02:18:26,638 --> 02:18:29,160
Take him to the healhouse!

1504
02:18:52,138 --> 02:18:54,680
When the truth gets revealed...

1505
02:18:54,740 --> 02:18:59,240
...this dagger will destoy the chest of
whoever tried to set us against each other!

1506
02:19:00,519 --> 02:20:54,550
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com